 conditions that can be improved through dietary changes, highlighting the importance of nutrition.AECOSAN:AECOSAN, or the Agencia Espa√±ola de Consumo, Seguridad Alimentaria y Nutrici√≥n, is the Spanish Agency for Food Safety and Nutrition. This agency is tasked with regulating food safety and ensuring that nutrition standards are upheld in Spain. Its primary role is to oversee and enforce regulations that protect consumers and promote public health related to food consumption.FEDERACI√ìN DE ASOCIACIONES DE CELIACOS DE ESPA√ëA:The "FEDERACI√ìN DE ASOCIACIONES DE CELIACOS DE ESPA√ëA" (FACE) is the leading organization in Spain dedicated to advocating for the rights and needs of individuals affected by celiac disease. This federation plays a crucial role in raising awareness and providing support for those with the condition. Additionally, FACE offers comprehensive information regarding gluten-free foods and dietary recommendations specifically tailored for celiac patients, ensuring they have access to the necessary resources to manage their health effectively.COMPLEJO HOSPITALARIO UNIVERSITARIO DE SANTIAGO:The Complex University Hospital of Santiago is a major healthcare facility in Santiago de Compostela, A Coru√±a, specializing in various medical fields including endocrinology.REGLAMENTO (CE) N¬∫ 834/2007:Reglamento (CE) n¬∫ 834/2007 is a regulation regarding the production and labeling of organic products in the European Union.MANUAL DE ETIQUETADO DE PRODUCTOS ECOL√ìGICOS:The Manual de etiquetado de productos ecol√≥gicos is a guide published by the Junta de Andaluc√≠a concerning the labeling of organic products.FUNDACI√ìN VASCA PARA LA SEGURIDAD AGROALIMENTARIA:Fundaci√≥n Vasca para la Seguridad Agroalimentaria (ELIKA) focuses on food safety and innovation in the Basque Country.REGLAMENTO DE EJECUCI√ìN (CE) NO. 828/2014:GRUPOS POBLACIONALES SUSCEPTIBLES:Los grupos poblacionales susceptibles incluyen ancianos, pacientes oncol√≥gicos y hospitalizados, quienes tienen un mayor riesgo de desnutrici√≥n.BISTRIAN B:Bistrian B is an author who co-authored research on malnutrition syndromes and their continuum in clinical settings.ROUBENOFF R:Roubenoff R is a researcher and author who has made significant contributions to the understanding of sarcopenia and its implications for the elderly. In addition to his work on sarcopenia, he is also involved in researching malnutrition syndromes and their clinical implications, highlighting the importance of nutrition in the health and well-being of older adults.HEIMBURGER DC:Heimburger DC is an author who contributed to the understanding of malnutrition syndromes in clinical practice.MALNUTRITION SYNDROMES:Malnutrition syndromes refer to a range of conditions that arise from inadequate nutrition, impacting clinical outcomes and healthcare costs.BRITISH ASSOCIATION OF PARENTERAL AND ENTERAL NUTRITION:The British Association of Parenteral and Enteral Nutrition (BAPEN) is an organization that developed the MUST screening tool for malnutrition.NUTRITIONAL SCREENING METHODS:Nutritional screening methods are tools used to identify individuals at risk of malnutrition, allowing for early intervention.ANTHROPOMETRIC PARAMETERS:Anthropometric parameters are measurements of the human body used in nutritional assessment to evaluate body composition and nutritional status.BIOCHEMICAL PARAMETERS:Biochemical parameters involve laboratory tests that assess nutritional status through the analysis of blood and other bodily fluids.FUNCTIONAL PARAMETERS:Functional parameters assess the physical capabilities of individuals, which can be affected by nutritional status.COSTS OF CARE:Costs of care refer to the financial implications associated with treating patients, which can be influenced by their nutritional status.MINI NUTRITIONAL ASSESSMENT SHORT FORM:Mini Nutritional Assessment Short Form is a validated independent screening tool based on the long version of the MNA, designed to reduce assessment time and can be used regularly in various patient settings.COMMUNITY:The community refers to a group of individuals living in a common area, where nutritional assessments can also be applied.VGS-GP:The VGS-GP is a variation of the original VGS method, designed for use in oncology patients to assess nutritional status with patient involvement.BAKER:Baker is a prominent researcher known for significant contributions to the field of nutrition. He co-authored a study focused on sucrose digestion in patients, enhancing the understanding of carbohydrate metabolism. Additionally, Baker played a key role in the development of the Global Subjective Assessment method, which is utilized for nutritional evaluation, providing a comprehensive approach to assessing an individual's nutritional status. Furthermore, he is recognized for developing the classic VGS method in the 1980s, which has been instrumental in evaluating nutritional status. Through these contributions, Baker has made a lasting impact on nutritional research and assessment methodologies.DUTCH MALNUTRITION STEERING GROUP:The Dutch Malnutrition Steering Group is an organization dedicated to addressing malnutrition issues within the Netherlands. It plays a crucial role in developing the SNAQ (Screening Nutritional Assessment Questionnaire) and its various validated versions tailored for different patient populations. Through its initiatives, the group aims to improve nutritional care and outcomes for individuals at risk of malnutrition.M√âTODO DE CARDONA:The Cardona method is a nutritional screening tool for hospitalized patients that evaluates recent weight changes and other clinical factors.M√âTODO DE ELMORE:The Elmore method is a numerical scale for assessing nutritional risk based on multivariate equations related to serum albumin and weight loss.M√âTODO CONUT:The CONUT method is an automated nutritional screening tool developed in Spain that alerts healthcare providers about potential malnutrition risks.PAR√ÅMETROS DE LABORATORIO:Los par√°metros de laboratorio son datos bioqu√≠micos que se utilizan en la valoraci√≥n nutricional para establecer un diagn√≥stico.MEDIDAS ANTROPOM√âTRICAS:Las medidas antropom√©tricas son datos que se recogen para evaluar el estado nutricional de un individuo.DATOS SOCIALES:Los datos sociales, como econ√≥micos y laborales, son relevantes en la valoraci√≥n nutricional de un paciente.CLINICAL DATA:Clinical data refers to the medical information collected about a patient, including recent weight loss, mental state, and systemic diseases that may interfere with nutrition.SOCIAL HISTORY:Social history encompasses the socioeconomic factors affecting a patient's health, such as income level, education, physical activity, and cultural practices.ANTHROPOMETRIC MEASUREMENTS:Anthropometric measurements are non-invasive assessments used to evaluate a patient's body composition and nutritional status, including weight, height, and body mass index.PHYSICAL EXAMINATION:Physical examination is a thorough assessment of a patient's physical condition, particularly in cases of malnutrition, to identify signs and symptoms related to nutritional deficiencies.MENTAL STATE:Mental state refers to the psychological condition of a patient, which can impact their nutritional intake and overall health.SYSTEMIC DISEASES:Systemic diseases are health conditions that can interfere with a patient's ability to maintain proper nutrition, such as cancer or organ failures.TOXIC CONSUMPTION:Toxic consumption includes the intake of harmful substances like alcohol or drugs, which can adversely affect nutritional status.DIETARY SURVEY:A dietary survey is a method used to gather information about a patient's food intake and dietary habits, often used in nutritional assessments.ALASTR√öE A:Alastru√© A is an author who contributed to the study on geriatric population and nutritional assessment.ESQUIUS M:Esquius M is an author who contributed to the study on geriatric population and nutritional assessment.GELANCH J:Gelanch J is an author who contributed to the study on geriatric population and nutritional assessment.GONZ√ÅLEZ F:Gonz√°lez F is an author who contributed to the study on geriatric population and nutritional assessment.RUZAFA A:Ruzafa A is an author who contributed to the study on geriatric population and nutritional assessment.PASTOR M:Pastor M is an author who contributed to the study on geriatric population and nutritional assessment.X CONGRESO DE LA SOCIEDAD DE NUTRIC:X Congreso de la Sociedad de Nutric is a conference where the assessment of weight and height in bedridden patients was discussed.POBLACI√ìN GERI√ÅTRICA:Poblaci√≥n geri√°trica refers to the elderly population that is the focus of the nutritional assessment study.TALL√çMETRO:Tall√≠metro is a device used for measuring height, important in the assessment of nutritional status.B√ÅSQUILA:B√°squila refers to the scale used for measuring weight, which is essential in nutritional assessments.B√ÅSICA:SOCIEDAD DE NUTRICI√ìN Y DIET√âTICA DE GALICIA:The Society of Nutrition and Dietetics of Galicia is an organization that focuses on nutritional assessment and guidelines in Galicia, Spain.M. POBLACI√ìN:Pastor M. Poblaci√≥n is a professional involved in geriatric nutritional assessment and standards.ALASTR√öE:Alastru√© is a reference for nutritional standards in Spain, particularly for the elderly population.ESQUIUS:Esquius is another reference for nutritional standards in Spain, specifically including elderly populations.X CONGRESO DE LA SOCIEDAD DE NUTRICI√ìN Y DIET√âTICA DE GALICIA:The X Congress of the Society of Nutrition and Dietetics of Galicia held in La Coru√±a in May 2000 focused on nutritional assessment for bedridden patients.SOCIETY OF NUTRITION AND DIETETICS OF GALICIA:GERIATRIC NUTRITIONAL ASSESSMENT:Geriatric nutritional assessment focuses on evaluating the nutritional needs and status of elderly patients, ensuring they receive appropriate care.CIRCUNFERENCIA DEL BRAZO:The "CIRCUNFERENCIA DEL BRAZO" refers to a measurement utilized in nutritional assessment to evaluate muscle mass and overall nutritional status. This measurement is taken at the midpoint of the non-dominant arm, serving as an important indicator for assessing body composition.CIRCUNFERENCIA MUSCULAR DEL BRAZO:The "CIRCUNFERENCIA MUSCULAR DEL BRAZO" is a measurement used to assess the muscle mass of individuals, particularly in the context of nutritional evaluations. This measurement is significant as it can indicate changes in muscle mass, which may decrease in cases of malnutrition. Thus, the circumferential measurement of the arm serves as an important tool in evaluating an individual's nutritional status and overall health.PROTE√çNAS PLASM√ÅTICAS:"PROTE√çNAS PLASM√ÅTICAS" se refiere a las prote√≠nas presentes en el plasma sangu√≠neo, cuya concentraci√≥n es un indicador clave del estado del compartimento proteico visceral. Estas prote√≠nas son fundamentales en la evaluaci√≥n nutricional, ya que se miden durante las valoraciones nutricionales para determinar el estado nutricional de los pacientes.RBP:RBP, or retinol-binding protein, is a crucial protein that plays a significant role in the transport of vitamin A within the body. It binds to retinol, which is essential for nutritional assessment and overall health. RBP is characterized by its short half-life, indicating that it is rapidly metabolized in the body. This protein is vital for maintaining adequate levels of vitamin A, which is important for various physiological functions, including vision, immune response, and cellular communication.CARDONA:Cardona is a method used for nutritional assessment in hospitalized patients.UL√çBARRI:Ul√≠barri is an automated method for assessing nutritional risk.CHANG:Chang is a diagnostic test for assessing nutritional status.DYNAMOMETRY:Dynamometry is a method used to measure muscle strength, often employed in nutritional assessments.ISOTOPIC DILUTION TECHNIQUES:Isotopic dilution techniques are methods used to assess body composition and nutritional status.BIOELECTRICAL IMPEDANCE:Bioelectrical impedance is a method and technique utilized to assess body composition and nutritional status. It is particularly effective in evaluating body composition in malnourished patients, providing valuable insights into their nutritional health.ALIANZA M√ÅSNUTRIDOS:Alianza M√°snutridos is a coalition in Spain dedicated to tackling malnutrition associated with disease through a multidisciplinary approach. The organization focuses on implementing screening processes at various levels of healthcare to identify and address malnutrition effectively. Additionally, Alianza M√°snutridos aims to raise awareness and integrate the issue of malnutrition into national and regional health strategies, ensuring that it is recognized as a critical component of public health initiatives.SOCIEDAD ESPA√ëOLA DE NUTRICI√ìN ENTERAL Y PARENTERAL:The "Sociedad Espa√±ola de Nutrici√≥n Enteral y Parenteral" (SENPE) is a professional organization dedicated to the promotion and development of enteral and parenteral nutrition in Spain. It focuses on providing resources and support for clinical nutrition, particularly for patients with specific needs such as renal insufficiency and those undergoing hemodialysis. SENPE publishes guidelines and studies that address various aspects of nutritional support, including the administration and absorption of medications in patients receiving enteral nutrition. Through its efforts, SENPE aims to enhance the quality of nutritional care and ensure that healthcare professionals have access to the latest information and best practices in the field of enteral and parenteral nutrition.CONSEJO DE EUROPA:The Consejo de Europa is an international organization dedicated to promoting human rights, democracy, and the rule of law across Europe. In 2003, the Consejo de Europa issued recommendations specifically addressing the issue of hospital malnutrition, which included the establishment of guidelines aimed at guiding future actions in this critical area.HOLANDA:Holland has successfully implemented programs to combat malnutrition since 2007, aiming to gradually reduce its prevalence across all healthcare levels.NUTRITION DAY:Nutrition Day is an initiative organized by ESPEN that focuses on evaluating the nutrition of patients admitted to hospitals in order to assess the prevalence of malnutrition. This initiative aims to raise awareness and address the issue of malnutrition across Europe, highlighting its significance in healthcare settings.CONSEJO GENERAL DE ENFERMER√çA:The Consejo General de Enfermer√≠a is the governing body for nursing professionals in Spain, promoting nursing standards and practices.ALIANZA GENERAL DE PACIENTES:The Alianza General de Pacientes is an organization in Spain that represents patient interests and advocates for their rights in healthcare.SOCIEDAD ESPA√ëOLA DE MEDICINA DE FAMILIA Y COMUNITARIA:The Sociedad Espa√±ola de Medicina de Familia y Comunitaria (semFYC) is a professional society for family medicine practitioners in Spain.SOCIEDAD ESPA√ëOLA DE M√âDICOS DE ATENCI√ìN PRIMARIA:The Sociedad Espa√±ola de M√©dicos de Atenci√≥n Primaria (SEMERGEN) is an organization focused on the interests and education of primary care physicians in Spain.SOCIEDAD ESPA√ëOLA DE GASTROENTEROLOG√çA, HEPATOLOG√çA Y NUTRICI√ìN PEDI√ÅTRICA:The Sociedad Espa√±ola de Gastroenterolog√≠a, Hepatolog√≠a y Nutrici√≥n Pedi√°trica (SGHNP) is a professional society dedicated to pediatric gastroenterology and nutrition in Spain.SOCIEDAD ESPA√ëOLA DE ONCOLOG√çA RADIOTER√ÅPICA:The Sociedad Espa√±ola de Oncolog√≠a Radioter√°pica (SEOR) is an organization focused on the field of radiation oncology in Spain.FUNDACI√ìN ABBOTT:Fundaci√≥n Abbott is a foundation that supports health and nutrition initiatives, particularly in relation to malnutrition.SOCIEDAD ESPA√ëOLA DE DIRECTIVOS DE SALUD:The Sociedad Espa√±ola de Directivos de Salud (SEDISA) is an organization representing health executives and managers in Spain.CONSEJO GENERAL DE COLEGIOS OFICIALES DE FARMAC√âUTICOS:SOCIEDAD ESPA√ëOLA DE ONCOLOG√çA RADIOTERAP√âTICA:HOLAND√âS:El Ministerio de Sanidad holand√©s ha estado involucrado en la lucha contra la desnutrici√≥n en el pa√≠s desde 2007.COSTE DE HOSPITALIZACI√ìN:El coste de hospitalizaci√≥n es un factor importante en la evaluaci√≥n de la desnutrici√≥n, ya que los pacientes desnutridos generan un gasto adicional diario.BRAUN:Braun is a company recognized for its innovative contributions to health and personal care, particularly through the development of nutritional assessment tools. Additionally, Braun is a manufacturer that specializes in producing nutritional solutions, which encompass a range of products, including parenteral nutrition offerings. This dual focus on both assessment and nutritional solutions highlights Braun's commitment to enhancing health and well-being through advanced technology and quality products.BURGOS PEL√ÅEZ R:Burgos Pel√°ez R is an author who contributed to the literature on malnutrition and disease.SULLIVAN DH:Sullivan DH is an author who studied the impact of nutrition status on morbidity and mortality in geriatric patients.VANITALLIE TB:Vanitallie TB is an author who has researched frailty in the elderly and its relation to nutrition.AGARWAL N:Agarwal N is an author who investigated the predictive ability of nutritional variables for mortality in elderly people.P√âREZ DE LA CRUZ A:P√©rez de la Cruz A is an author who studied malnutrition in hospitalized patients.CAMBRIDGE, UK:Cambridge, UK is the location of Cabi Publishing, which published works on disease-related malnutrition.COLLABORATIVE GROUP FOR THE STUDY OF HOSPITAL MALNUTRITION IN GALICIA:A group focused on studying hospital malnutrition in Galicia, Spain, and conducting nutritional status studies of inpatients.NUTRITIONDAY:An international event aimed at raising awareness about nutrition and malnutrition.FIGHT AGAINST MALNUTRITION:An initiative aimed at combating malnutrition through various strategies and awareness campaigns.NUTRITIONAL STATUS STUDY OF INPATIENTS IN HOSPITALS OF GALICIA:A study conducted to assess the nutritional status of inpatients in hospitals across Galicia, Spain.J NUTRITION HEALTH AGING:A journal that publishes research related to nutrition and health in aging populations.NUTR BURBANK LOS ANGEL CTY CALIF:A publication that discusses various aspects of nutrition, including screening and assessment tools.HOSPITAL UNIVERSITARIO VIRGEN DE LA VICTORIA:Hospital Universitario Virgen de la Victoria is a hospital situated in M√°laga, Spain. It is known for conducting research in the fields of endocrinology and nutrition.VALORACI√ìN DE LA INGESTA:Assessment of intake refers to the evaluation of dietary habits and nutrient intake of individuals or populations.ELMADFA & MEYER:Elmadfa & Meyer are researchers who contributed to the study of population dietary intake and public health policy recommendations in 2014.WILLETT WC.:Willett WC. is a researcher known for studying food intake and its implications on nutritional status since 1998.SURVEY METHODS:Survey methods are tools used to estimate dietary intake at individual or collective levels, crucial for nutritional studies.NUTRITIONAL EDUCATION:Nutritional education is essential for successful dietary interventions and improving patient outcomes.ENCUESTAS DIET√âTICAS:Encuestas diet√©ticas are methods and surveys utilized to collect data on dietary intake, serving both individual and collective assessments. These surveys are essential for evaluating dietary habits and the nutritional intake of patients, playing a crucial role in managing nutritional health.ENCUESTAS NUTRICIONALES:Encuestas nutricionales are methods used to assess dietary intake and nutritional status of individuals or populations.SERIA MAJEM LL:Serra Majem Ll is an author referenced in the context of nutritional epidemiology and survey methods.RECORDATORIO DE 24 HORAS:The "RECORDATORIO DE 24 HORAS" is a dietary assessment tool utilized to evaluate an individual's food intake, which is particularly important for managing obesity. This method involves individuals recalling all foods and beverages they have consumed over the past 24 hours. It serves as a retrospective dietary assessment technique that quantifies food and beverage intake, providing valuable insights into dietary habits and nutritional status.CUESTIONARIO DE FRECUENCIA DE CONSUMO:The "Cuestionario de Frecuencia de Consumo" is a survey method designed to evaluate how frequently specific foods are consumed within a defined time frame. It serves as a predefined questionnaire that assesses habitual food intake, allowing for a comprehensive analysis of dietary patterns. This tool is instrumental in measuring dietary intake over a specified period, providing valuable insights into individuals' eating habits.ENCUESTAS FAMILIARES:Encuestas familiares are surveys conducted to gather dietary information from households.HOJAS DE BALANCE ALIMENTARIO:Hojas de balance alimentario are tools used to assess food supply and consumption in a population.REGISTRO DIET√âTICO:ARANCETA B:Aranceta B is an author referenced in the document, contributing to the discussion on dietary assessment methods.REGISTRO/DIARIO DIET√âTICO:The Registro/Diario Diet√©tico is a method for recording food and beverage intake over a specified period, often used in dietary assessments.M√âTODOS DE EVALUACI√ìN DE LA INGESTA DE ALIMENTOS:This refers to various methods for assessing food intake, including the 24-hour recall, dietary records, and food frequency questionnaires.PUNTO CLAVE:A key point in determining the type of questionnaire to be used based on available resources and interviewer capabilities.M√âTODO DE VALORACI√ìN DE LA INGESTA:A method for assessing dietary intake, which can be useful if preceded by careful design and planning.LIMITACIONES:Refers to the limitations associated with different dietary assessment methods that need to be considered.CUESTIONARIO ABIERTO-CERRADO:A type of questionnaire format that can be used in dietary assessments.ENTREVISTADOR:Refers to the interviewer who may administer certain dietary assessment methods.AUTADMINISTRADO:Refers to self-administered questionnaires that can be used in dietary assessments.SUBJETIVO:Refers to the subjective nature of certain dietary assessment methods.COSTE:COSTE refers to the financial expenditure associated with healthcare interventions, which is a critical factor in analyses of cost-effectiveness and cost-utility. Additionally, COSTE encompasses the costs associated with various dietary assessment methods. This dual focus highlights the importance of understanding both healthcare and dietary costs in evaluating overall health interventions and their economic implications.COOPERACI√ìN:Refers to the level of cooperation required from participants in dietary assessments.RECURSOS DISPONIBLES:IENVA:IENVA is an online platform and organization dedicated to providing individuals with tools for nutritional analysis and dietary record-keeping. It offers access to comprehensive food composition databases and nutritional information, enabling users to track their food intake and understand the nutritional composition of their meals. Additionally, IENVA features a food composition table and a nutritional analysis program that includes detailed reporting, making it a valuable resource for those looking to manage their diet effectively.HERN√ÅNDEZ:Hern√°ndez is a researcher noted for contributions to the study of dietary intake methods, with a particular focus on the 24-hour recall method. Additionally, Hern√°ndez (2010) is referenced in the text concerning the food consumption frequency questionnaire, indicating the relevance of their work in the field of dietary assessment and nutrition research.GIBSON:Gibson is a researcher who has studied dietary assessment methods, including the use of household measures and food models in dietary recalls.CUESTIONARIO DE FRECUENCIA DE CONSUMO DE ALIMENTOS:A questionnaire designed to gather data on food consumption frequency over a specific time period, including variations by season and special occasions.SHIM ET AL.:Shim et al. are researchers noted for their contributions to dietary assessment methodologies. In their 2014 study, they highlighted the effectiveness of the 24-hour recall method for evaluating dietary intake. Additionally, they provided valuable insights into the administration of dietary questionnaires, further enhancing the understanding of dietary assessment techniques.MARGETTS & NELSON:Margetts & Nelson (1997) is a reference cited in discussions regarding the limitations of dietary assessment methods. They are recognized as researchers who have made significant contributions to the methodology of dietary assessment, enhancing the understanding and application of these methods in nutritional research.HTTP://WWW.CHOOSEMYPLATE.GOV/:A website providing dietary guidelines and resources for healthy eating.HTTP://WWW.SEH-LELHA.ORG/CALENA.ASPX:A website offering tools and resources for dietary assessment and nutrition.HTTP://WWW.IENVA.ORG/CALCDIETA/:A website that provides dietary calculation tools and resources.HUEVOS, CARNES, PESCADOS:A category of food items that includes eggs, meats, and fish, which are part of the food frequency questionnaire.LECHE ENTERA:LECHE ENTERA, or whole milk, is a dairy product that is included in dietary plans and is also listed in food frequency questionnaires. It serves as a significant component in various nutritional guidelines, highlighting its importance in a balanced diet.LECHE SEMIDESNATADA:LECHE SEMIDESNATADA refers to semi-skimmed milk, which is a moderate-fat dairy product. It is commonly included in food frequency questionnaires, indicating its relevance in dietary assessments. This type of milk offers a balance between full-fat and skim milk, making it a popular choice for those seeking a lower fat option while still enjoying the taste and nutritional benefits of milk.LECHE DESCREMADA:Leche descremada, also known as skim milk, is a lower-fat milk option that is commonly consumed. It is a dairy product that is often included in food frequency questionnaires, highlighting its relevance in dietary assessments.LECHE CONDENSADA:Condensed milk, a dairy product listed in the food frequency questionnaire.NATA O CREMA DE LECHE:Cream, a dairy product listed in the food frequency questionnaire.BATIDOS DE LECHE:Milkshakes, a dairy product listed in the food frequency questionnaire.YOGURT ENTERO:Whole yogurt, a dairy product listed in the food frequency questionnaire.YOGURT DESCREMADO:Skimmed yogurt, a dairy product listed in the food frequency questionnaire.PETIT SUISSE:A type of soft cheese, listed in the food frequency questionnaire.REQUET√ìN O CUAJADA:Cottage cheese, a dairy product listed in the food frequency questionnaire.QUESO EN PORCIONES O CREMOSO:Portion cheese or creamy cheese, a dairy product listed in the food frequency questionnaire.QUESOS CURADOS, SEMICURADOS:Cured and semi-cured cheeses, listed in the food frequency questionnaire.QUESO BLANCO O FRESCO:Fresh cheese, a dairy product listed in the food frequency questionnaire.NATILLAS, FLAN, PUDING:Custards, flans, and puddings, listed in the food frequency questionnaire.HUEVOS DE GALLINA:Chicken eggs, listed in the food frequency questionnaire.POLLO O PAVO CON PIEL:Chicken or turkey with skin, listed in the food frequency questionnaire.POLLO O PAVO SIN PIEL:The entity "POLLO O PAVO SIN PIEL" refers to chicken or turkey that is prepared without skin. This option is included in the food frequency questionnaire, indicating its relevance in dietary assessments. Additionally, skinless chicken or turkey is permitted in modified diets, making it a suitable choice for individuals seeking healthier protein options.CARNE DE TERNERA O VACA:Beef, listed in the food frequency questionnaire.CARNE DE CERDO:Pork, listed in the food frequency questionnaire.CARNE DE CORDERO:CARNE DE CORDERO, or lamb, is a type of meat that is noted for its higher phosphorus content compared to other meats, which makes it less recommended for certain dietary considerations. Despite this, lamb is included in food frequency questionnaires, indicating its relevance in dietary assessments and consumption patterns.CONEJO O LIEBRE:Rabbit or hare, listed in the food frequency questionnaire.OTRAS V√çSCERAS:Other organ meats, listed in the food frequency questionnaire.)<|COMPLETE|>CFC:CFC is a method used for dietary assessment that does not modify the habits of the person surveyed and is relatively easy to develop.RIBEFOOD:Ribefood is an interactive web application designed for dietary adherence surveys.ENCUESTA DE ADHERENCIA A LA DIETA MEDITERR√ÅNEA:The Encuesta de Adherencia a la Dieta Mediterr√°nea is a survey designed to assess adherence to the Mediterranean diet.NUTRIENTE:NUTRIENTE refers to the nutrients that are investigated in dietary studies to understand their impact on health.DIETISTA-NUTRICIONISTA:A Dietitian-Nutritionist is a trained health professional specializing in nutrition and dietetics. They conduct dietary interviews to gather detailed information about individuals' eating habits and provide guidance on the appropriate intake of foods and liquids. In a clinical setting, a dietitian-nutritionist works under the supervision of a physician to manage dietary needs and meal planning, particularly in hospitals. Their role is essential in advising patients on how to maintain a balanced diet and make informed food choices to support their health.RED MEATS:Red meats are consumed less frequently in the Mediterranean diet, emphasizing lower intake for health benefits.DIETARY HISTORY:Dietary history refers to the process of assessing an individual's eating habits and fluid intake over time, with a particular focus on identifying foods that may contribute to health issues such as kidney stone formation. This method involves gathering detailed information about a patient's dietary practices, which can provide valuable insights for healthcare professionals in understanding and managing potential dietary-related health concerns.OLIVE OIL:FORO ACT√öA:Foro Act√∫a is a web resource that provides information and tools for modifying dietary habits, particularly for patients with overweight and obesity.MATAIX J:Mataix J is an author of a classic food composition table in the national context.MOREIRAS-VARELA O:Moreiras-Varela O is an author of a classic food composition table in the national context.AND√öJAR MM:And√∫jar MM is an author of a classic food composition table in the national context.CSIC:The Spanish National Research Council (CSIC) is involved in the development of food composition tables.TABLAS DE COMPOSICI√ìN DE ALIMENTOS:TABLAS DE COMPOSICI√ìN DE ALIMENTOS, or Food Composition Tables, are comprehensive compilations of data that detail the nutritional composition of a wide variety of foods. These tables provide essential information regarding the nutritional content of foods, including specific nutrients such as phosphorus levels. They serve as a valuable resource for understanding the dietary contributions of different foods and are utilized in nutrition research, dietary planning, and food labeling.BASES DE DATOS DE ALIMENTOS:Food Databases are digital collections of nutritional information about food items.APLICACIONES M√ìVILES:Mobile Applications are software tools that provide nutritional information and dietary tracking for users.CUESTIONARIO DE H√ÅBITOS:UNITED STATES DEPARTMENT OF AGRICULTURE:The United States Department of Agriculture (USDA) is a government agency that provides comprehensive food composition databases, including nutritional information about various food items.DIETOWIN:DIETOWIN¬Æ is a nutritional analysis software developed by Biol√≥gica Tecnolog√≠a M√©dica, S.L. that helps in analyzing dietary intake and creating personalized diets.DIETSOURCE:DIETSOURCE¬Æ is a nutritional analysis program developed by Nestl√© Consumer Health, designed to assist in dietary assessments and planning. This user-friendly software is particularly beneficial for dietitians, providing them with the tools necessary to conduct thorough dietary evaluations and create effective nutrition plans.EASYDIET:EASYDIET¬Æ is a nutritional analysis tool that can be used for dietary assessments and personalized diet creation.NUTRITIONAL DATABASES:Nutritional databases are collections of data that provide information on the nutritional composition of various food items, used for dietary analysis and research.NUTRITIONAL ANALYSIS:Nutritional analysis is a process that evaluates the nutritional content of food items to ensure that products meet the initial nutritional proposal and comply with established nutritional ranges. This analysis often involves the use of software tools and databases to assess dietary intake, providing a comprehensive understanding of the nutritional value of various foods.NUTRITIONAL INFORMATION:Nutritional information includes data about the nutrients contained in food items, such as macronutrients, vitamins, and minerals, essential for dietary planning and health.NUTRITIONAL TOOLS:Nutritional tools are resources, including software and online platforms, that assist individuals and professionals in analyzing dietary intake and planning diets.DIETARY INTAKE:Dietary intake refers to the total amount of food and drink consumed by an individual, which is analyzed for nutritional content and health implications.NUTRITIONAL DATABASE:Nutritional databases are collections of data that provide information on the nutritional composition of various food items, used for dietary analysis and research.)<|COMPLETE|>FORO ACTUA:FORO ACTUA is a web platform that offers interactive nutritional analysis, recipe analysis, and dietary habits surveys.MYFITNESSPAL:Myfitnesspal is a multi-format platform (web and apps) that provides an uncontrolled food table and exercise logging.DIETSTAT:DIETSTAT is a program used at Hospital Carlos Haya in M√°laga for dietary analysis and patient intake assessment.NUTRISOL:NUTRISOL is a program from the Department of Preventive Medicine at the University of M√°laga for nutritional analysis.MALAGA:M√°laga is a city in Spain where the Hospital Carlos Haya is located, which utilizes the DIETSTAT program.KOREA:Korea is a country where the Diet Evaluation System (DES) was developed for standardized face-to-face dietary interviews.NIH:The National Institutes of Health (NIH) is an organization that has highlighted key points in the management of celiac disease. Additionally, the NIH is involved in developing projects focused on dietary evaluation technologies, indicating its commitment to advancing research and improving health outcomes related to dietary conditions.CAMEMBERT:Camembert is a soft cheese from France, also classified under Dairy and Egg Products, recognized for its rich flavor and creamy interior.CARAWAY CHEESE:Caraway cheese is a type of cheese flavored with caraway seeds, falling under the Dairy and Egg Products category.CHEDDAR:Cheddar is a popular hard cheese originating from England, known for its sharp taste and versatility in cooking, classified under Dairy and Egg Products.CHESHIRE CHEESE:Cheshire cheese is a traditional English cheese known for its crumbly texture and distinct flavor, categorized under Dairy and Egg Products.COLBY:Colby is a semi-hard cheese from the United States, recognized for its mild flavor and open texture, classified under Dairy and Egg Products.COTTAGE CHEESE:Cottage cheese is a fresh cheese curd product with a mild flavor, categorized under Dairy and Egg Products, often used in various dishes.CREAM CHEESE:Cream cheese is a soft, spreadable cheese made from milk and cream, classified under Dairy and Egg Products, commonly used in desserts and spreads.EDAM:Edam is a semi-hard cheese originating from the Netherlands, known for its mild flavor and red wax coating, categorized under Dairy and Egg Products.BRIE:ROCHE:Roche is a pharmaceutical company involved in the development of the GoCARB Project, which is related to dietary assessment.GO CARB PROJECT:The GoCARB Project is an initiative by Roche aimed at improving dietary assessment methods.DIETARY DATA RECORD SYSTEM:The Dietary Data Record System (DDRS) is a project that integrates sensor technology for real-time recording of food intake.FOOD INTAKE RECORDING SOFTWARE SYSTEM:The Food Intake Recording Software System (FIRSST) is a project designed to assist in dietary assessment.IMPROVING DIETARY ASSESSMENT METHODS USING THE CELL PHONE AND DIGITAL IMAGING:This project focuses on enhancing dietary assessment methods through the use of mobile technology and digital imaging.AUTOMATED SELF-ASSISTED 24-HOUR DIETARY RECALL:The Automated Self-Assisted 24-h Dietary Recall (ASA24) is a system that helps individuals recall their dietary intake over a 24-hour period.MOBILE FOOD INTAKE VISUALIZATION AND VOICE RECOGNIZER:The Mobile Food Intake Visualization and Voice Recognizer (FIVR) is a project aimed at improving dietary assessment through mobile technology.REGISTER DIET√âTICO FOTOGR√ÅFICO:The Registro Diet√©tico Fotogr√°fico (RDF) is a method of dietary assessment that uses photographic records of food intake.ARAB ET AL.:Arab et al. is a reference to researchers who have worked on dietary assessment methods using images.GREGORY ET AL.:Gregory et al. is a reference to researchers involved in the development of dietary assessment technologies.KIKUNAGA ET AL.:Kikunaga et al. is a reference to researchers who have contributed to the field of dietary assessment.PORCA ET AL.:Porca et al. is a reference to researchers who have studied the impact of technology on dietary assessment.GEMMING ET AL.:NUEVAS TECNOLOG√çAS:Nuevas tecnolog√≠as refer to the advancements in technology that facilitate the assessment and management of dietary intake in clinical practice.PATOLOG√çA METAB√ìLICA Y NUTRICIONAL:Patolog√≠a metab√≥lica y nutricional encompasses various health conditions related to diet and nutrition that require clinical management.GIBSON RS:Gibson RS is an author and expert in nutritional assessment, particularly in measuring food consumption.M√âTODOS NUTRICIONALES:M√©todos nutricionales are techniques and approaches used to assess and improve dietary habits and nutritional health.RECURSOS INFORM√ÅTICOS:Recursos inform√°ticos are technological tools and resources that support dietary assessment and clinical practice.EVALUACI√ìN DE LA INGESTA:COMPLEJO HOSPITALARIO DE NAVARRA:The Complejo Hospitalario de Navarra is a hospital located in Pamplona, responsible for providing clinical nutrition and dietetic services.DIETA HOSPITALARIA:"DIETA HOSPITALARIA" refers to a structured dietary plan specifically designed for patients in a hospital setting. This dietary protocol is crucial for patient recovery and management, as it focuses on meeting the nutritional needs and restrictions based on individual medical conditions. The planning of hospital diets involves careful consideration of various dietary restrictions and guidelines to ensure that patients receive proper nutrition, which is essential for their health management and overall recovery.SECCI√ìN NUTRICI√ìN CL√çNICA Y DIET√âTICA:The Clinical Nutrition and Dietetics section is responsible for planning and managing dietary needs in the hospital.COCINA:Cocina refers to the kitchen facilities in a hospital, which play a crucial role in meal preparation and service for patients.T√âCNICO SUPERIOR EN DIET√âTICA:A professional responsible for planning and calibrating dietary menus in a hospital setting, ensuring nutritional quality.PROGRAMAS INFORM√ÅTICOS:Software systems used in hospitals to manage dietary requests and meal planning efficiently.C√ÅMARAS FRIGOR√çFICAS:Refrigeration units in hospitals that store prepared meals at safe temperatures to ensure food safety.MEN√öS:Menus are the planned lists of meals provided to patients, tailored to their dietary needs.SECCI√ìN DE ALIMENTACI√ìN:A department within the hospital that collaborates with dietitians to ensure meal quality.PERSONAL DE ENFERMER√çA:The "Personal de Enfermer√≠a" refers to the nursing staff responsible for various critical functions in patient care. This group includes both nurses and nursing assistants who are tasked with placing catheters and managing venous access in patients. Additionally, they play a vital role in translating dietary guidelines and monitoring patient intake within hospital settings. Their responsibilities encompass both technical procedures and patient education, ensuring comprehensive care for individuals under their supervision.M√âDICOS:M√©dicos are doctors who assess patients' nutritional status and collaborate with the Unidad de Nutrici√≥n for dietary needs.RESOLUCI√ìN RES AP (2003) 3:A resolution by the Council of Europe regarding food and nutritional care in hospitals, establishing recommendations for improving patient care.REGLAMENTO 1169/2011:A regulation in the European Union that sets legal standards for food information to consumers, including nutritional labeling in collective dining settings like hospitals.ISO 22000:2005:ISO 22000:2005 is an international standard that ensures food safety based on the APPCC system and is similar in structure to ISO 9000.GU√çA DE PR√ÅCTICAS CORRECTAS DE HIGIENE Y MANIPULACI√ìN:A document that outlines the fundamental hygiene requirements for food operations to ensure food safety.AN√ÅLISIS MICROBIOL√ìGICOS:Microbiological analyses conducted periodically on food and surfaces in hospitals to ensure safety and hygiene.SEGURIDAD ALIMENTARIA:Food safety practices aimed at preventing foodborne illnesses and ensuring the health of consumers, particularly in hospital settings.PERSONAL DE COCINA:Kitchen staff responsible for food preparation and ensuring hygiene standards are met in hospital kitchens.TOXIINFECCIONES ALIMENTARIAS:HOSPITAL DIET:The "HOSPITAL DIET" encompasses a systematic approach to diet planning for hospitalized patients, focusing on their unique physiological and pathological conditions. It involves the selection of appropriate dietary plans that cater to the specific health needs of patients, particularly after surgeries such as bariatric surgery. Hospital diets are structured meal plans designed to effectively manage nutritional intake, especially for individuals with specific health conditions like diabetes. These nutritional plans and protocols are established to ensure that patients receive the necessary dietary support during their hospital stay, taking into account their dietary restrictions and health requirements.DIETAS PROGRESIVAS:"DIETAS PROGRESIVAS" refers to a series of dietary plans specifically designed to support recovery and adapt to changes in a patient's condition following surgery or during medical treatment. These progressive diets are utilized to aid in the restoration of digestive function after a period of fasting, ensuring that patients can gradually reintroduce food in a manner that is safe and conducive to their healing process.DIETAS ESPECIALES:Special diets are non-coded diets tailored to individual patient needs.NUTRIENT DISTRIBUTION:Nutrient distribution in hospital diets typically consists of 50-55% carbohydrates, 30-35% lipids, and 10-20% proteins.DIETARY RESTRICTIONS:Dietary restrictions are essential for managing the health of patients with adrenoleucodistrofia, primarily aimed at limiting the intake of very long-chain fatty acids. In addition to this specific restriction, dietary guidelines for these patients may also encompass a variety of other limitations, including gluten-free, low-purine, and vegetarian options. These comprehensive dietary restrictions are designed to support the overall well-being and nutritional needs of individuals affected by this condition.ODONTOLOGICAL/FAÃÅCIL MASTICACI√ìN:Odontological/easy chewing diets are tailored for patients with chewing or swallowing difficulties.HIPERPROTEICA:HIPERPROTEICA refers to a high-protein diet specifically designed for patients who require an increased protein intake. This includes individuals suffering from conditions such as burns or those experiencing metabolic stress, where the body‚Äôs protein needs are elevated. The Hiperproteica diet is particularly beneficial for patients with burns or increased catabolism, as it helps support recovery and maintain muscle mass during periods of heightened protein demand.DIAB√âTICA NI√ëOS PEQUE√ëOS:Diabetic diets for small children are designed for children under 6 years with diabetes.DIAB√âTICA NI√ëOS GRANDES:Diabetic diets for older children are tailored for children over 6 years with diabetes.CEL√çACA:Cel√≠aca diets are gluten-free diets for patients with gluten intolerance.POBRE EN COLESTEROL:Pobre en colesterol diets are low-cholesterol diets aimed at patients with dyslipidemia.LAXANTE:Laxante diets are designed for patients suffering from constipation.NO CARNE:No carne diets are for patients with meat intolerance.F√ÅCIL DIGESTI√ìN:LUNES:Lunes is the Spanish word for Monday, representing the first day of the week in the diet plan.MARTES:Martes is the Spanish word for Tuesday, representing the second day of the week in the diet plan.MI√âRCOLES:Mi√©rcoles is the Spanish word for Wednesday, representing the third day of the week in the diet plan.JUEVES:Jueves is the Spanish word for Thursday, representing the fourth day of the week in the diet plan.VIERNES:Viernes is the Spanish word for Friday, representing the fifth day of the week in the diet plan.S√ÅBADO:S√°bado is the Spanish word for Saturday, representing the sixth day of the week in the diet plan.DOMINGO:Domingo is the Spanish word for Sunday, representing the seventh day of the week in the diet plan.LECHE DESNATADA:Leche Desnatada is skim milk, a low-fat dairy product included in the diet plan for breakfast.BOLLER√çA:Boller√≠a refers to a variety of baked goods, commonly known as pastries, which are often included in breakfast options within certain diet plans. These baked goods may contain high levels of fructose and sorbitol, which can affect individuals with specific intolerances. While some pastries can vary in gluten content, making them potentially suitable for gluten-free diets, it is important to note that pastries are not permitted in modified diets. Dietary guidelines suggest that pastries should be consumed occasionally and in moderation.LENTEJAS ESTOFADAS:Lentejas Estofadas are a nutritious dish made from stewed lentils, often served as a first course in various diet plans. This dish is particularly notable for its high fiber content, making it a suitable option for those following a laxative diet. The combination of lentils provides not only essential nutrients but also promotes digestive health, aligning with dietary recommendations for increased fiber intake.FIDEOS A LA CAZUELA:Fideos a la cazuela are noodles cooked in a casserole style, served as a first course.POTAJE DE GARBANZOS:Potaje de Garbanzos is a chickpea stew that serves as a nutritious first course option in various diet plans. This dish is particularly notable for its inclusion in the laxative diet, as it is made with chickpeas, which are high in fiber. The high fiber content of chickpeas contributes to digestive health, making Potaje de Garbanzos a beneficial choice for those seeking to improve their dietary habits.ARROZ CON MEJILLONES Y CALAMAR:Arroz con Mejillones y Calamar is rice with mussels and squid, served as a first course.BERZA CON PATATAS:Berza con Patatas is a dish made of greens and potatoes, included in the first course options.GUISANTES PRIMAVERA:Guisantes Primavera refers to spring peas that are typically served as a first course. This dish is notable for its inclusion in a laxative diet, as it is made with spring peas that are high in 