p to partially hydrolyze lactose, making it more tolerable for individuals who are lactose intolerant. This fermentation process not only improves lactose digestion but also enhances the overall nutritional profile of the yogurt.

Yogur contains 2.2 mg of iron per 100 grams and has a glycemic index of 51, indicating its moderate impact on blood sugar levels. It is also a good source of calcium, which is essential for bone health, and is recommended for daily intake. Additionally, yogur is beneficial for gut health, particularly during episodes of diarrhea, as it contains probiotics that support digestive function.

Furthermore, yogur is a soft food option suitable for patients with dysphagia, although caution is advised when mixing it with fruits due to potential risks. Overall, yogur is a nutritious and versatile food that can be enjoyed by a wide range of individuals, contributing positively to their dietary needs.NATILLAS:Natillas are a type of custard-like dessert that is included in various dessert options. This dessert may contain ingredients that some individuals with dietary restrictions need to avoid, making it important for those with specific dietary needs to check the ingredients before consumption.ARROZ CON LECHE:Arroz con Leche is rice pudding, served as a dessert option.HELADO:Helado is ice cream, included in the dessert options.FLAN:FLAN is a type of caramel custard dessert that is commonly served as a dessert option. However, it may contain ingredients that some individuals with dietary restrictions need to avoid.CUAJADA:Cuajada is a gluten-free curd dessert that is included in the low-purine diet. It is recognized as a type of curd dessert and is featured among the dessert options available.LECHE CON DESCAFEINADO:Leche con Descafeinado is decaffeinated milk, served as a snack option.ENSALADA DE ARROZ:Ensalada de Arroz is a rice salad, served as a first course for dinner.CREMA DE ESP√ÅRRAGOS:Crema de Esp√°rragos is asparagus cream soup, included in the first course options for dinner.SOPA DE PESCADO:Sopa de Pescado is fish soup, served as a first course for dinner.PUR√â DE PATATAS Y ZANAHORIA:Pur√©e de Patatas y Zanahoria is a mashed potato and carrot dish, included in the first course options for dinner.ENSALADA CAMPERA:"ENSALADA CAMPERA" is a gluten-free country-style salad that is included in gluten-free diets and various dietary plans. This rustic salad is typically served as a first course for dinner, highlighting its role as a wholesome and versatile dish suitable for those seeking gluten-free options.MENESTRA SALTEADA CON JAM√ìN:Menestra Salteada con Jam√≥n is saut√©ed vegetables with ham, included in the first course options for dinner.JUD√çAS VERDES CON TOMATE:Jud√≠as Verdes con Tomate is green beans with tomato, served as a first course for dinner.FOGONERO ANDALUZA:Fogonero Andaluza is a dish from Andalusia, served as a second course for dinner.EMPANADILLAS DE BONITO:Empanadillas de Bonito are small tuna pastries, included in the second course options for dinner.TORTILLA DE JAM√ìN:Tortilla de Jam√≥n is a ham omelet that is included in dietary recommendations and is typically served as a second course for dinner.PLATIJA ROMANA:PlatiJa Romana is a Roman-style flatfish dish, included in the second course options for dinner.AT√öN ENCEBOLLADO:At√∫n Encebollado is tuna cooked with onions, served with rice pilaf as a second course.PECHUGA VILLAROY:Pechuga Villaroy is a breaded chicken breast dish, included in the second course options for dinner.JAM√ìN AL HORNO:Jamon al Horno is baked ham, served with broccoli and carrots as a second course.HUEVOS GRAT√âN:Huevos Graten are baked eggs, included in the second course options for dinner.FILETE DE ABADEJO:Filete de Abadejo is a fillet of coley fish, served with carrots as a second course.RAPE EN SALSA MARINERA:Rape en Salsa Marinera is monkfish in a marinara sauce, included in the second course options for dinner.SALCHICHAS AL VINO:Salchichas al V("entity"TORTILLA DE CALABAC√çN:Tortilla de Calabac√≠n is a gluten-free zucchini omelet that is part of the gluten-free meal plan and included in dietary recommendations. This dish serves as a nutritious option within the second course selections for dinner, highlighting its versatility and suitability for those seeking gluten-free meal choices.LENGUADO A LA MENI√àRE:Lenguado a la Meni√®re is sole fish prepared in a classic French style, served as a second course.HUEVOS EN SALSA:Huevos en Salsa are eggs served in a sauce, included in the second course options for dinner.DIETA SEMIL√çQUIDA:The "DIETA SEMIL√çQUIDA" is recognized as the second step in dietary progression. It consists of a combination of liquid and pasty foods, which are designed to stimulate digestion more effectively than a strictly liquid diet. This dietary approach serves as a transitional phase, allowing individuals to gradually reintroduce more solid foods while still maintaining a focus on easily digestible options.DIETA SEMIBLANDA:The "DIETA SEMIBLANDA" is a dietary phase that follows the semiliquid diet, characterized by the inclusion of soft foods that are easier to chew and digest. This diet serves as a transitional step in the progression of dietary intake, introducing solid foods while assessing the individual's tolerance to protein and encouraging the process of chewing.DIETA BLANDA:"Dieta blanda" is a dietary phase characterized by the inclusion of soft foods that are easy to digest, making it particularly suitable for patients recovering from surgery. It serves as a progression from the semi-soft diet and is indicated for individuals experiencing digestive alterations. This diet encompasses a variety of solid textures, ensuring that it meets the nutritional needs of those who may have difficulty with more complex foods.GALLETAS:Galletas, commonly known as cookies, are a type of baked good that can vary significantly in their gluten content. While some galletas may be suitable for gluten-free diets, many traditional varieties contain gluten, making them unsuitable for individuals with celiac disease. Galletas are often consumed as a snack, providing enjoyment and energy, and they are included in various dietary recommendations. Nutritionally, galletas contain approximately 2 mg of iron per 100 grams. However, it is important to note that some galletas can be hard and may fragment easily, which poses risks for patients with dysphagia, a condition that affects swallowing. Overall, galletas are a versatile snack option, but considerations regarding gluten content and texture are essential for certain dietary needs.MERENDA:Merienda is a light meal or snack typically consumed in the afternoon. It often includes items such as galletas (cookies) and leche (milk). This tradition emphasizes a casual and enjoyable break during the day, allowing individuals to recharge with simple yet satisfying food options.DESAYUNO:Desayuno refers to breakfast, the first meal of the day, which is essential for providing the necessary energy and nutrients to start the day. This meal can include a variety of specific items tailored for dietary management and restrictions, making it suitable for patients with particular health needs. Common components of a traditional desayuno may include leche (milk), pan (bread), and mermelada (jam), as well as other foods such as dairy products, cereals, and fruit. These items are important for meeting nutritional requirements and ensuring a balanced diet.DIETA DE TRANSICI√ìN:La dieta de transici√≥n es el √∫ltimo paso en la progresi√≥n diet√©tica, que incluye todos los grupos de alimentos y resulta en una dieta variada y equilibrada.DIETA DE F√ÅCIL MASTICACI√ìN:The "DIETA DE F√ÅCIL MASTICACI√ìN" is a specialized diet intended for patients who experience difficulties with chewing or salivating. This diet comprises a diverse, complete, and balanced array of soft-textured foods, ensuring that individuals can meet their nutritional needs despite their chewing challenges. It is specifically designed to accommodate the dietary requirements of those with masticatory or salivary issues, promoting both health and comfort in eating.PUR√â DE VERDURA:El pur√© de verdura es un alimento que se incluye en las dietas semil√≠quidas y semiblandas, facilitando la digesti√≥n y la masticaci√≥n.PESCADO AL HORNO:El pescado al horno es un tipo de alimento que se introduce en la dieta semiblanda, siendo una fuente de prote√≠na magra.FRUTA EN ALM√çBAR:La fruta en alm√≠bar es un tipo de postre que se incluye en las dietas semiblandas y blandas, proporcionando un sabor dulce y nutrientes.DIETAS CON MODIFICACI√ìN DE TEXTURA:Diets that involve changing the texture of food to accommodate patients with swallowing difficulties or other dietary restrictions.DIETA ODONTOLOGICA:A diet designed for patients with dental issues, focusing on soft foods that are easy to chew and swallow.QUESO FRESCO:QUESO FRESCO is a type of fresh cheese that is known for its soft and crumbly texture. It is often used in various culinary applications, particularly in Mexican cuisine. However, it is important to note that fresh cheese can be sticky, which may pose a risk for patients with dysphagia, a condition that affects swallowing. Therefore, caution should be exercised when serving QUESO FRESCO to individuals with this condition.CARAMELLOS:Candies that can be sticky and difficult to swallow, posing risks for patients with swallowing difficulties.HUEVO DURO:Hard-boiled eggs are a food that can be difficult to swallow without sauce, making them risky for patients with dysphagia.BISCOITOS:Biscuits are a type of food that can easily fragment, posing a risk for patients with swallowing difficulties.PATATAS CHIPS:Patatas chips, commonly known as potato chips, are a popular snack food characterized by their high fat and salt content. While they are enjoyed by many for their taste and crunch, it is important to note that these chips can easily fragment, which poses a risk for individuals with swallowing difficulties.BOMBONES RELLENOS:Filled chocolates that can release liquids when chewed, posing risks for patients with dysphagia.ACEITUNAS:Aceitunas, or olives, are a staple in Mediterranean diets and are recognized for their numerous health benefits. They are rich in oleic acid, which contributes to their nutritional value and association with healthy eating patterns. While aceitunas can be enjoyed in various culinary applications, it is important to note that they may contain pits, which can pose a risk for individuals with swallowing difficulties. Overall, aceitunas are a versatile food that plays a significant role in Mediterranean cuisine.UVAS:UVAS refers to grapes, a type of fruit that offers some dietary fiber. However, it is important to note that grapes can pose a choking hazard for patients with dysphagia, a condition that affects swallowing. Therefore, while UVAS can be a nutritious addition to the diet, caution should be exercised when they are consumed by individuals with swallowing difficulties.SAND√çA:Sand√≠a, commonly known as watermelon, is a type of fruit recognized for its high water content and sweetness. It is often enjoyed in various forms, including fresh slices, juiced, or incorporated into desserts. Additionally, Sand√≠a contains a higher amount of galactose, which can be a consideration for certain dietary needs. It is important to note that watermelon can have seeds, which may pose a risk for individuals with swallowing difficulties.ESP√ÅRRAGOS:Esp√°rragos, or asparagus, are vegetables known for their nutritional benefits but also have certain characteristics that may pose risks for specific individuals. They contain hard fibers, which can be problematic for patients with dysphagia, a condition that makes swallowing difficult. Additionally, esp√°rragos have moderate purine levels, which can influence uric acid levels in the body, potentially affecting individuals with conditions such as gout. Therefore, while esp√°rragos can be a healthy addition to many diets, caution is advised for those with swallowing difficulties or issues related to uric acid.PUERROS:Puerros, commonly known as leeks, are a type of vegetable that contribute to dietary fiber intake. However, they are characterized by having hard fibers, which may pose a risk for patients with dysphagia, a condition that affects swallowing. Therefore, while puerros can be a nutritious addition to a diet, caution should be exercised when consumed by individuals with swallowing difficulties.FIBRAS DURAS:Hard fibers in foods that can pose risks for patients with swallowing difficulties.GRUMOS:Lumps in food that can pose risks for patients with dysphagia.HUESOS:HUESOS, or bones, are essential structures in the body that play a crucial role in providing support and protection to various organs. They are dependent on copper for their development and maintenance, highlighting the importance of this mineral in bone health. Additionally, certain types of bones can pose a choking hazard for patients with dysphagia, a condition that affects swallowing. This dual aspect of bones emphasizes their significance in both physiological functions and potential health risks.ESPINAS:Fish bones that can pose a choking hazard for patients with dysphagia.PEPITAS:Seeds that can pose a choking hazard for patients with dysphagia.CALDO VEGETAL:CALDO VEGETAL, or vegetable broth, is permitted in modified diets as part of the beverage group. It is particularly suitable for patients with swallowing difficulties, making it an important dietary option for those requiring specific nutritional considerations.MACEDONIA TRITURADA:Chopped fruit salad that is pureed for patients with swallowing difficulties.ACEITE OLIVA:ACEITE OLIVA is a type of oil characterized by its nutritional composition, which includes 13.5% saturated fats, 73.7% monounsaturated fats, and 8.4% polyunsaturated fats. This oil is particularly noted for its versatility, as it can be incorporated into diets for patients with swallowing difficulties, making it a suitable option for those requiring specific dietary considerations.CEREALES DEXTRINADOS:Dextrin cereals that can be included in diets for patients with swallowing difficulties.TORTILLA FRANCESA:The "TORTILLA FRANCESA" is a versatile dish that can be described as a gluten-free Spanish omelet, making it suitable for those following a gluten-free meal plan. Additionally, it is recognized as a French omelet that can be included in diets for patients with swallowing difficulties, highlighting its adaptability for various dietary needs.CHAMPIGNONES:Mushrooms that can be included in diets for patients with swallowing difficulties.MERIENDA:Merienda is an afternoon snack that plays a significant role in children's diets, typically comprising approximately 10-15% of their total caloric intake. This snack not only serves as a source of energy but also contributes to the daily nutritional needs of children. Additionally, merienda can be tailored to include specific items for dietary management, making it suitable for individuals with dietary restrictions. Overall, merienda is an important component of a balanced diet, providing both nourishment and enjoyment during the afternoon hours.COMIDA:Comida is recognized as the main meal of the day, playing a crucial role in contributing significantly to the total energy value of the diet. It is particularly important for individuals with dietary restrictions, as lunch can be tailored to include specific foods that meet their nutritional needs.CENA:CENA refers to the evening meal, which is an important part of daily nutrition. It should be balanced to meet the remaining nutritional needs of the day, ensuring that individuals receive adequate nourishment. For patients with dietary restrictions, CENA can include specific foods tailored to their needs, allowing for a safe and enjoyable dining experience. Additionally, for children, dinner should constitute approximately 25% of their total energy value for the day, highlighting its significance in their overall dietary intake.ALIMENTACI√ìN CON NUTRICI√ìN ARTIFICIAL:The use of artificial nutrition methods to provide essential nutrients to patients who cannot consume food normally.M√ìDULOS DE PROTE√çNAS EN POLVO:Protein powder supplements used to enhance the protein content of meals for patients with specific dietary needs.PACIENTES CON QUEMADURAS:Patients suffering from severe burns who require specialized dietary plans to support healing and recovery.DIETA DE HEMODI√ÅLISIS:A specific diet designed for patients undergoing hemodialysis, focusing on protein and mineral restrictions.DIETA 40 G/60 G PROTE√çNAS:A dietary plan providing either 40 or 60 grams of protein, used for patients with renal and hepatic conditions.DIETAS CONTROL PROTEICO:Dietary plans specifically designed to manage protein intake for patients with various medical conditions.UPP CATAB√ìLICOS:A condition related to increased protein breakdown in the body, often requiring dietary adjustments.T√âCNICAS DEPURACI√ìN EXTRARRENAL:Methods used to remove waste products from the blood in patients with kidney failure, influencing dietary needs.DIETA HEMODI√ÅLISIS:A specific dietary regimen for patients undergoing hemodialysis, focusing on protein and mineral restrictions.DIETAS HIPOPROTEICAS:Dietas dise√±adas para reducir la ingesta de prote√≠nas y as√≠ disminuir las concentraciones de urea en sangre y el s√≠ndrome ur√©mico en pacientes con enfermedad renalHEPATOPAT√çA CR√ìNICA:HEPATOPAT√çA CR√ìNICA, or chronic liver disease, is a medical condition characterized by long-term damage to the liver, which can result in liver dysfunction and potentially lead to liver failure. This condition often necessitates nutritional support due to the risk of malnutrition, which may arise from the disease itself. Patients with HEPATOPAT√çA CR√ìNICA may experience complications such as malnutrition, encephalopathy, and sarcopenia, highlighting the importance of adequate nutritional intervention, including enteral feeding, to maintain health and manage the disease effectively.INSULIN THERAPY:Insulin therapy is a treatment for diabetes that involves administering insulin to control blood sugar levels, often requiring specific dietary adjustments.FIBER SOLUBLE:Soluble fiber is a type of fiber that can help regulate blood sugar levels and is recommended for diabetic diets.DIETARY RECOMMENDATIONS:Dietary recommendations encompass a variety of guidelines aimed at promoting overall health and managing specific medical conditions through balanced nutrition. These recommendations are designed to prevent atherosclerosis and enhance cardiovascular health, ensuring individuals maintain a heart-healthy diet. For patients with chronic kidney disease, dietary recommendations focus on managing phosphorus levels to support kidney function. 

In the context of bariatric surgery, dietary recommendations provide essential guidelines for patients to follow post-operation, helping them achieve proper nutrition and maintain weight loss effectively. For individuals with Glycogen Storage Disease Type VI (GSDVI), dietary recommendations emphasize a high carbohydrate intake along with a slightly elevated protein intake to manage symptoms and sustain energy levels.

For those managing diabetes, dietary recommendations include guidelines that prioritize low sugar and high fiber intake to help regulate blood sugar levels. Additionally, these recommendations suggest a gradual reintroduction of lactose to assess tolerance in individuals who may be lactose intolerant. Furthermore, it is advised to limit foods high in fructose and sorbitol, particularly in processed products, to alleviate symptoms of intolerance. Overall, dietary recommendations serve as a crucial framework for individuals to achieve optimal health and manage specific dietary needs effectively.MEAL PLANS:Meal plans are structured dietary guidelines that help diabetic patients manage their food intake effectively.DIABETIC PATIENTS:Diabetic patients are individuals diagnosed with diabetes mellitus who require specific dietary management to control their condition.OBSTETRICIA:Obstetricia is the field of medicine that deals with childbirth and the care of women giving birth, which may include dietary management during pregnancy.ALUBIAS VERDES:Alubias verdes con patatas is a dish included in the laxative diet, consisting of green beans with potatoes, providing dietary fiber.MENESTRA DE VERDURAS:Menestra de verduras is a dish included in the laxative diet, consisting of a variety of vegetables, providing dietary fiber.PLANTAS DE GERIATR√çA:Plantas de geriatr√≠a are healthcare facilities that focus on elderly patients, often implementing specialized diets.TABLA 10:Tabla 10 refers to a specific table that details the content and distribution of carbohydrates in a diet of 1800 calories. Additionally, it includes a table that shows the contributions of vitamins in parenteral nutrition according to the age of pediatric patients. This comprehensive overview highlights both the carbohydrate distribution in a caloric context and the vitamin requirements tailored for different age groups in pediatric care.TABLA 11:Tabla 11 refers to a specific table outlining the components of a laxative diet.DIETA LAAXANTE:DIETA POBRE EN RESIDUO:The "DIETA POBRE EN RESIDUO" is a specialized dietary regimen aimed at minimizing fecal volume to reduce the risk of intestinal obstruction, particularly indicated for patients with specific medical conditions. This low-residue diet is designed to limit the amount of undigested food that passes through the intestines, making it particularly beneficial for individuals suffering from certain gastrointestinal disorders. By focusing on reducing residue, the diet helps manage symptoms and improve overall digestive health for those affected.DIETA SIN RESIDUO:A diet designed to cleanse the intestines by excluding foods that form fecal matter, also indicated for specific medical tests.DIETA CONTROLADA EN GRASAS:A diet that regulates fat intake, used for diagnosing malabsorption and other related conditions.ACELGA CON PATATA:"ACELGA CON PATATA" is a dish that consists of Swiss chard and potatoes. It is recognized for its inclusion in various dietary plans, making it a versatile option for those seeking healthy meal choices. Additionally, this dish is gluten-free, making it suitable for individuals following a gluten-free diet.ENSALADA VERDE VARIADA:A varied green salad included in dietary recommendations.ENSALADA DE TOMATE Y QUESO FRESCO:The "ENSALADA DE TOMATE Y QUESO FRESCO" is a gluten-free salad that features a combination of fresh tomatoes and cheese. It is suitable for individuals following a gluten-free diet and is also included in various dietary plans. This salad is recognized for its simplicity and freshness, making it a versatile option for those seeking healthy meal choices.ENSALADA DEL CHEF:A chef's salad included in dietary recommendations.BORRAJA CON PATATA:"BORRAJA CON PATATA" is a dish that combines borage and potatoes, making it a nutritious option included in dietary recommendations. It is also gluten-free, which allows it to be part of a gluten-free meal plan, catering to those with gluten sensitivities or celiac disease. This dish not only highlights the unique flavor of borage but also provides a wholesome and healthy choice for various dietary needs.JUD√çAS VERDES CON PATATA:A dish made of green beans and potatoes, included in dietary plans.HUEVOS AL GRAT√âN:A dish of baked eggs, included in dietary recommendations.TOMATE ASADO:TOMATE ASADO is a gluten-free roasted tomato dish that is suitable for individuals following a gluten-free diet. It is often included in various dietary plans, making it a versatile option for those seeking healthy and flavorful meal choices.ABADEJO A LA GALLEGA:"ABADEJO A LA GALLEGA" is a dish of cod prepared in the traditional Galician style. It is recognized for its inclusion in dietary recommendations, highlighting its nutritional value. Additionally, this dish is gluten-free, making it suitable for those following a gluten-free meal plan.GUISANTES:Guisantes, commonly known as peas, are legumes that are valued for their sweet flavor and nutritional benefits. They are a gluten-free food, making them suitable for individuals following a gluten-free diet. Guisantes provide a notable amount of iron, offering 1.7 mg per 100 grams. Due to their versatility and health benefits, they are frequently included in various dietary plans.PLATIJA A LA ROMANA:A dish of sole prepared in the Roman style, included in dietary recommendations.MENESTRA:A mixed vegetable dish included in dietary plans.JAM√ìN ASADO EN SALSA:JAM√ìN ASADO EN SALSA is a gluten-free roasted ham dish served with sauce, making it a suitable option for those following a gluten-free meal plan. This dish is also included in dietary recommendations, highlighting its nutritional value and compatibility with various dietary needs.PESCADILLA A LA MARINERA:A dish of fish prepared in a sailor's style, included in dietary recommendations.KIWI:Kiwi is a small, brown, fuzzy fruit characterized by its bright green flesh and tiny black seeds. It is renowned for its unique sweet and tangy flavor, 