refers to a dietary model that excludes gluten, which is essential for the health of individuals with celiac disease and those with non-celiac gluten sensitivity. This gluten-free diet involves the complete elimination of foods containing gluten grains, making it a crucial treatment for celiac patients. The diet is designed to be nutritionally complete and includes a variety of meals for each day of the week, encompassing breakfast, lunch, and dinner options. Overall, "DIETA SIN GLUTEN" serves as a vital dietary regimen tailored to meet the specific needs of those affected by gluten-related disorders.DIETA POBRE EN PURINAS:The "DIETA POBRE EN PURINAS" is a dietary model specifically designed to limit purine intake, primarily aimed at patients suffering from gout. This diet includes specific meal recommendations that help manage and reduce uric acid levels in individuals with hyperuricemia. In addition to dietary management, the low-purine diet emphasizes the importance of weight reduction as a means to further alleviate symptoms and improve overall health for those affected by these conditions.PACIENTES CEL√çACOS:Patients with celiac disease who require a gluten-free diet to avoid symptoms and complications.DIETA CON 100 GR DE GRASA:A diet that includes 100 grams of fat, which may be used for specific nutritional needs or conditions.DIETA POBRE EN GRASA:A low-fat diet is designed to limit fat intake, often recommended for patients with specific health conditions.DIETA OVO-LACTO-VEGETARIANA:A vegetarian diet that includes both eggs and dairy products, considered the most inclusive among vegetarian diets.DIETA PARA NEUTROPENIA:A specialized diet for patients undergoing chemotherapy or bone marrow transplants, aimed at reducing the risk of infection by avoiding high-risk foods.ALUBIAS VERDES CON PATATA:A gluten-free meal consisting of green beans and potatoes, featured in the gluten-free diet.POTAJES DE GARBANZOS:A gluten-free dish made with chickpeas, part of the glut