 DEL SUE√ëO:APNEA DEL SUE√ëO is a condition characterized by repeated interruptions in breathing during sleep, which can significantly affect overall health. It is often associated with obesity, making it a relevant consideration in the context of very low-calorie diets (VLCD). This relationship highlights the importance of addressing sleep apnea in individuals who are managing obesity, as it can be a comorbid condition that complicates health outcomes.TRASTORNOS PSICOL√ìGICOS:Psychological disorders can influence obesity treatment outcomes, as they may affect motivation and adherence to treatment plans.REGISTROS DIET√âTICOS:Dietary records are used to track food intake over time, aiding in the management of obesity.CUESTIONARIOS PREDEFINIDOS:Predefined questionnaires are tools used to assess dietary habits and energy intake, important for obesity treatment.BALANCE ENERG√âTICO:Energy balance refers to the relationship between calories consumed and calories expended, crucial for weight management.OBJETIVOS DE TRATAMIENTO:Treatment objectives are specific goals set for weight loss and health improvement in patients with obesity.)<|COMPLETE|>H√çGADO GRASO NO ALCOH√ìLICO:H√≠gado Graso No Alcoh√≥lico, also known as non-alcoholic fatty liver disease (NAFLD), is a medical condition characterized by the accumulation of fat in the liver. This condition typically occurs in individuals who consume little or no alcohol. It can be associated with various factors, including iron overload. The presence of excess fat in the liver can lead to further complications if not managed properly.APNEA OBSTRUCTIVA DEL SUE√ëO:Obstructive sleep apnea is a potentially serious sleep disorder in which breathing repeatedly stops and starts during sleep.ASTMA:Asthma is a condition in which your airways narrow and swell and may produce extra mucus, making breathing difficult.OSTEOARTRITIS:Osteoarthritis is a degenerative joint disease that occurs when the protective cartilage that cushions the ends of the bones wears down over time.INCONTINENCIA URINARIA:Urinary incontinence is the involuntary leakage of urine, which can be a result of various underlying conditions.DENSIDAD ENERG√âTICA:Energy density refers to the number of calories in a given volume or weight of food, influencing dietary choices and weight management.P√âNDULO DE PESO:Weight pendulum refers to the concept of maintaining a stable weight through balanced energy intake and expenditure.DIRECTIVA 98/6/CE:Directiva 98/6/CE es una regulaci√≥n de la Comisi√≥n Europea que establece normas sobre la composici√≥n, etiquetado y duraci√≥n de uso de productos de muy bajo contenido cal√≥rico.REAL DECRETO 1430/1997:El Real Decreto 1430/1997 es la incorporaci√≥n al ordenamiento jur√≠dico espa√±ol de la Directiva 98/6/CE, regulando productos de muy bajo contenido cal√≥rico.PACIENTES ADULTOS OBESOS:Pacientes adultos obesos son aquellos que tienen un √≠ndice de masa corporal (IMC) superior a 30 kg/m¬≤ y que han fracasado en intentos previos de p√©rdida de peso.ENFERMEDADES CARD√çACAS:Las enfermedades card√≠acas son condiciones que afectan el coraz√≥n y pueden ser contraindicaciones para el uso de dietas VLCD.SOBREPESO GRADO II:El sobrepeso grado II se refiere a un IMC superior a 27 kg/m¬≤ y puede estar asociado a comorbilidades que justifican el uso de dietas VLCD.TRASTORNOS PSIQUI√ÅTRICOS:TRASTORNOS PSIQUI√ÅTRICOS se refiere a condiciones de salud mental que pueden influir en el tratamiento y la nutrici√≥n de los pacientes. Estas condiciones son consideradas contraindicaciones para el uso de dietas de muy bajo contenido cal√≥rico (VLCD). Adem√°s, trastornos psiqui√°tricos como la depresi√≥n cl√≠nica son comunes en pacientes que padecen enfermedades cr√≥nicas severas, lo que puede afectar negativamente su ingesta nutricional.ANOREXIA/BULIMIA:La anorexia y la bulimia son trastornos alimentarios que son contraindicaciones para el uso de dietas VLCD.INGESTA CAL√ìRICA:La ingesta cal√≥rica se refiere a la cantidad de calor√≠as consumidas a trav√©s de los alimentos, que puede aumentar con alimentos de alta densidad energ√©tica.PALATABILIDAD:La palatabilidad se refiere a la aceptaci√≥n y el placer que se experimenta al consumir alimentos, a menudo influenciada por el contenido de grasa.ESTUDIOS DE INTERVENCI√ìN:Los estudios de intervenci√≥n son investigaciones que analizan el efecto de modificar la densidad energ√©tica en la dieta sobre la p√©rdida de peso.PRODUCTOS COMERCIALES:Los productos comerciales son alimentos dise√±ados para ser utilizados en dietas de muy bajo contenido cal√≥rico, como barritas y galletas.M√ÅS DE 12 KCAL/KG:M√°s de 12 kcal/kg se refiere a la cantidad de calor√≠as que se considera alta en comparaci√≥n con las dietas de muy bajo contenido cal√≥rico.M√ÅS BARATOS:Los alimentos energ√©ticamente m√°s densos suelen ser m√°s baratos, lo que puede influir en las decisiones de consumo.MOTIVOS DE SALUD:Los motivos de salud son razones que pueden justificar la necesidad de una p√©rdida de peso r√°pida, como condiciones m√©dicas.(N␀␀␀␀␀␀“N␀␀␀␀␀␀YO␀␀␀␀␀␀P␀␀␀␀␀␀ùP␀␀␀␀␀␀=Q␀␀␀␀␀␀ΩR␀␀␀␀␀␀U␀␀␀␀␀␀ÓU␀␀␀␀␀␀àV␀␀␀␀␀␀DW␀␀␀␀␀␀ÓW␀␀␀␀␀␀X␀␀␀␀␀␀ÕX␀␀␀␀␀␀LY␀␀␀␀␀␀«Z␀␀␀␀␀␀D[␀␀␀␀␀␀Ë[␀␀␀␀␀␀Ø\␀␀␀␀␀␀K]␀␀␀␀␀␀ı]␀␀␀␀␀␀ë^␀␀␀␀␀␀_␀␀␀␀␀␀±_␀␀␀␀␀␀®`␀␀␀␀␀␀,a␀␀␀␀␀␀≈a␀␀␀␀␀␀åd␀␀␀␀␀␀Sf␀␀␀␀␀␀Ûf␀␀␀␀␀␀îg␀␀␀␀␀␀5h␀␀␀␀␀␀‘h␀␀␀␀␀␀Vi␀␀␀␀␀␀”i␀␀␀␀␀␀êj␀␀␀␀␀␀=k␀␀␀␀␀␀l␀␀␀␀␀␀÷l␀␀␀␀␀␀am␀␀␀␀␀␀n␀␀␀␀␀␀ôn␀␀␀␀␀␀8o␀␀␀␀␀␀≠o␀␀␀␀␀␀p␀␀␀␀␀␀èp␀␀␀␀␀␀q␀␀␀␀␀␀sq␀␀␀␀␀␀‚q␀␀␀␀␀␀àr␀␀␀␀␀␀s␀␀␀␀␀␀~s␀␀␀␀␀␀Ôs␀␀␀␀␀␀˜s␀␀␀␀␀␀≥t␀␀␀␀␀␀#u␀␀␀␀␀␀íu␀␀␀␀␀␀v␀␀␀␀␀␀‚v␀␀␀␀␀␀w␀␀␀␀␀␀≈w␀␀␀␀␀␀Ùx␀␀␀␀␀␀øz␀␀␀␀␀␀:|␀␀␀␀␀␀6~␀␀␀␀␀␀ã~␀␀␀␀␀␀’~␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Ü␀␀␀␀␀␀Ä␀␀␀␀␀␀Å␀␀␀␀␀␀0É␀␀␀␀␀␀sÜ␀␀␀␀␀␀Êá␀␀␀␀␀␀Üà␀␀␀␀␀␀÷â␀␀␀␀␀␀|ä␀␀␀␀␀␀%ã␀␀␀␀␀␀Áã␀␀␀␀␀␀æå␀␀␀␀␀␀√ç␀␀␀␀␀␀ué␀␀␀␀␀␀è␀␀␀␀␀␀´è␀␀␀␀␀␀„è␀␀␀␀␀␀ê␀␀␀␀␀␀ìê␀␀␀␀␀␀Lë␀␀␀␀␀␀Mì␀␀␀␀␀␀∫ì␀␀␀␀␀␀;î␀␀␀␀␀␀¨î␀␀␀␀␀␀.ï␀␀␀␀␀␀ïï␀␀␀␀␀␀ñ␀␀␀␀␀␀Œñ␀␀␀␀␀␀.ó␀␀␀␀␀␀™ó␀␀␀␀␀␀Mò␀␀␀␀␀␀Ωò␀␀␀␀␀␀Bô␀␀␀␀␀␀ö␀␀␀␀␀␀£ö␀␀␀␀␀␀>õ␀␀␀␀␀␀ªõ␀␀␀␀␀␀Gú␀␀␀␀␀␀ƒú␀␀␀␀␀␀␀û␀␀␀␀␀␀èû␀␀␀␀␀␀ü␀␀␀␀␀␀Ÿ†␀␀␀␀␀␀≠¢␀␀␀␀␀␀£␀␀␀␀␀␀ö£␀␀␀␀␀␀Æ£␀␀␀␀␀␀*§␀␀␀␀␀␀“§␀␀␀␀␀␀ê•␀␀␀␀␀␀¶␀␀␀␀␀␀°¶␀␀␀␀