ãª¬à•º|ÓïºÎ=§ñô;ærSΩ˜lºÅ…ëª¶Œæ=˙N°º°´ºM¯ö<…(Àª'gÔºßbáº=><Æ∏HΩ‡Y‰<FÅåºﬂÊË<Ûﬂ‹ºhπ<ﬂQö<ßÔã8Tò¿ºîª¡<1™Îπ√$8Ω° +ºlØPºÛŸ<Îè<î.Ω<,‘ºbd
=6Æ~<•æ<©qïºAıº[z␀9Îz=ZúS<œM+=1<Tws<¬Mº•Ë«<vÚL<ü‰¥;UU Ω∫º<ÀîºØLëºÌ`Ñ<—Ö–ªÇmÓ<ÕFg<#I”;Û◊=v—ˇ;ØLë<'“ ªmCº0XΩºîpº¥;ñå<îªA∏+«•º:Âù<Eƒ,=hhùºÚ;␀º{"title": "NUTRICI\u00d3N CL\u00cdNICA Y METABOLISMO:Clinical Nutrition and Metabolism is a field of study and practice focused on the nutritional needs and metabolic processes of patients."}{"title": "FIABS:The Spanish Federation of Food and Beverage Industries (FIABS) represents the interests of the food and beverage sector in Spain."}{"title": "REGULACI\u00d3N DE LAS DECLARACIONES NUTRICIONALES:The regulation of nutritional claims aims to standardize how nutritional information is presented to avoid misleading consumers."}{"title": "NUEVA NORMATIVA:The new regulation refers to recent changes in food labeling laws that enhance the clarity and visibility of nutritional information."}{"title": "PATOLOG\u00cdAS ESPEC\u00cdFICAS:Specific pathologies refer to health conditions that can be improved through dietary changes, highlighting the importance of nutrition."}{"title": "AECOSAN:AECOSAN, or the Agencia Espa\u00f1ola de Consumo, Seguridad Alimentaria y Nutrici\u00f3n, is the Spanish Agency for Food Safety and Nutrition. This agency is tasked with regulating food safety and ensuring that nutrition standards are upheld in Spain. Its primary role is to oversee and enforce regulations that protect consumers and promote public health related to food consumption."}{"title": "FEDERACI\u00d3N DE ASOCIACIONES DE CELIACOS DE ESPA\u00d1A:The \"FEDERACI\u00d3N DE ASOCIACIONES DE CELIACOS DE ESPA\u00d1A\" (FACE) is the leading organization in Spain dedicated to advocating for the rights and needs of individuals affected by celiac disease. This federation plays a crucial role in raising awareness and providing support for those with the condition. Additionally, FACE offers comprehensive information regarding gluten-free foods and dietary recommendations specifically tailored for celiac patients, ensuring they have access to the necessary resources to manage their health effectively."}{"title": "COMPLEJO HOSPITALARIO UNIVERSITARIO DE SANTIAGO:The Complex University Hospital of Santiago is a major healthcare facility in Santiago de Compostela, A Coru\u00f1a, specializing in various medical fields including endocrinology."}{"title": "REGLAMENTO (CE) N\u00ba 834/2007:Reglamento (CE) n\u00ba 834/2007 is a regulation regarding the production and labeling of organic products in the European Union."}{"title": "MANUAL DE ETIQUETADO DE PRODUCTOS ECOL\u00d3GICOS:The Manual de etiquetado de productos ecol\u00f3gicos is a guide published by the Junta de Andaluc\u00eda concerning the labeling of organic products."}{"title": "FUNDACI\u00d3N VASCA PARA LA SEGURIDAD AGROALIMENTARIA:Fundaci\u00f3n Vasca para la Seguridad Agroalimentaria (ELIKA) focuses on food safety and innovation in the Basque Country."}{"title": "REGLAMENTO DE EJECUCI\u00d3N (CE) NO. 828/2014:"}{"title": "GRUPOS POBLACIONALES SUSCEPTIBLES:Los grupos poblacionales susceptibles incluyen ancianos, pacientes oncol\u00f3gicos y hospitalizados, quienes tienen un mayor riesgo de desnutrici\u00f3n."}{"title": "BISTRIAN B:Bistrian B is an author who co-authored research on malnutrition syndromes and their continuum in clinical settings."}{"title": "ROUBENOFF R:Roubenoff R is a researcher and author who has made significant contributions to the understanding of sarcopenia and its implications for the elderly. In addition to his work on sarcopenia, he is also involved in researching malnutrition syndromes and their clinical implications, highlighting the importance of nutrition in the health and well-being of older adults."}{"title": "HEIMBURGER DC:Heimburger DC is an author who contributed to the understanding of malnutrition syndromes in clinical practice."}{"title": "MALNUTRITION SYNDROMES:Malnutrition syndromes refer to a range of conditions that arise from inadequate nutrition, impacting clinical outcomes and healthcare costs."}{"title": "BRITISH ASSOCIATION OF PARENTERAL AND ENTERAL NUTRITION:The British Association of Parenteral and Enteral Nutrition (BAPEN) is an organization that developed the MUST screening tool for malnutrition."}{"title": "NUTRITIONAL SCREENING METHODS:Nutritional screening methods are tools used to identify individuals at risk of malnutrition, allowing for early intervention."}{"title": "ANTHROPOMETRIC PARAMETERS:Anthropometric parameters are measurements of the human body used in nutritional assessment to evaluate body composition and nutritional status."}{"title": "BIOCHEMICAL PARAMETERS:Biochemical parameters involve laboratory tests that assess nutritional status through the analysis of blood and other bodily fluids."}{"title": "FUNCTIONAL PARAMETERS:Functional parameters assess the physical capabilities of individuals, which can be affected by nutritional status."}{"title": "COSTS OF CARE:Costs of care refer to the financial implications associated with treating patients, which can be influenced by their nutritional status."}{"title": "MINI NUTRITIONAL ASSESSMENT SHORT FORM:Mini Nutritional Assessment Short Form is a validated independent screening tool based on the long version of the MNA, designed to reduce assessment time and can be used regularly in various patient settings."}{"title": "COMMUNITY:The community refers to a group of individuals living in a common area, where nutritional assessments can also be applied."}{"title": "VGS-GP:The VGS-GP is a variation of the original VGS method, designed for use in oncology patients to assess nutritional status with patient involvement."}{"title": "BAKER:Baker is a prominent researcher known for significant contributions to the field of nutrition. He co-authored a study focused on sucrose digestion in patients, enhancing the understanding of carbohydrate metabolism. Additionally, Baker played a key role in the development of the Global Subjective Assessment method, which is utilized for nutritional evaluation, providing a comprehensive approach to assessing an individual's nutritional status. Furthermore, he is recognized for developing the classic VGS method in the 1980s, which has been instrumental in evaluating nutritional status. Through these contributions, Baker has made a lasting impact on nutritional research and assessment methodologies."}{"title": "DUTCH MALNUTRITION STEERING GROUP:The Dutch Malnutrition Steering Group is an organization dedicated to addressing malnutrition issues within the Netherlands. It plays a crucial role in developing the SNAQ (Screening Nutritional Assessment Questionnaire) and its various validated versions tailored for different patient populations. Through its initiatives, the group aims to improve nutritional care and outcomes for individuals at risk of malnutrition."}{"title": "M\u00c9TODO DE CARDONA:The Cardona method is a nutritional screening tool for hospitalized patients that evaluates recent weight changes and other clinical factors."}{"title": "M\u00c9TODO DE ELMORE:The Elmore method is a numerical scale for assessing nutritional risk based on multivariate equations related to serum albumin and weight loss."}{"title": "M\u00c9TODO CONUT:The CONUT method is an automated nutritional screening tool developed in Spain that alerts healthcare providers about potential malnutrition risks."}{"title": "PAR\u00c1METROS DE LABORATORIO:Los par\u00e1metros de laboratorio son datos bioqu\u00edmicos que se utilizan en la valoraci\u00f3n nutricional para establecer un diagn\u00f3stico."}{"title": "MEDIDAS ANTROPOM\u00c9TRICAS:Las medidas antropom\u00e9tricas son datos que se recogen para evaluar el estado nutricional de un individuo."}{"title": "DATOS SOCIALES:Los datos sociales, como econ\u00f3micos y laborales, son relevantes en la valoraci\u00f3n nutricional de un paciente."}{"title": "CLINICAL DATA:Clinical data refers to the medical information collected about a patient, including recent weight loss, mental state, and systemic diseases that may interfere with nutrition."}{"title": "SOCIAL HISTORY:Social history encompasses the socioeconomic factors affecting a patient's health, such as income level, education, physical activity, and cultural practices."}{"title": "ANTHROPOMETRIC MEASUREMENTS:Anthropometric measurements are non-invasive assessments used to evaluate a patient's body composition and nutritional status, including weight, height, and body mass index."}{"title": "PHYSICAL EXAMINATION:Physical examination is a thorough assessment of a patient's physical condition, particularly in cases of malnutrition, to identify signs and symptoms related to nutritional deficiencies."}{"title": "MENTAL STATE:Mental state refers to the psychological condition of a patient, which can impact their nutritional intake and overall health."}{"title": "SYSTEMIC DISEASES:Systemic diseases are health conditions that can interfere with a patient's ability to maintain proper nutrition, such as cancer or organ failures."}{"title": "TOXIC CONSUMPTION:Toxic consumption includes the intake of harmful substances like alcohol or drugs, which can adversely affect nutritional status."}{"title": "DIETARY SURVEY:A dietary survey is a method used to gather information about a patient's food intake and dietary habits, often used in nutritional assessments."}{"title": "ALASTR\u00daE A:Alastru\u00e9 A is an author who contributed to the study on geriatric population and nutritional assessment."}{"title": "ESQUIUS M:Esquius M is an author who contributed to the study on geriatric population and nutritional assessment."}{"title": "GELANCH J:Gelanch J is an author who contributed to the study on geriatric population and nutritional assessment."}{"title": "GONZ\u00c1LEZ F:Gonz\u00e1lez F is an author who contributed to the study on geriatric population and nutritional assessment."}{"title": "RUZAFA A:Ruzafa A is an author who contributed to the study on geriatric population and nutritional assessment."}{"title": "PASTOR M:Pastor M is an author who contributed to the study on geriatric population and nutritional assessment."}{"title": "X CONGRESO DE LA SOCIEDAD DE NUTRIC:X Congreso de la Sociedad de Nutric is a conference where the assessment of weight and height in bedridden patients was discussed."}{"title": "POBLACI\u00d3N GERI\u00c1TRICA:Poblaci\u00f3n geri\u00e1trica refers to the elderly population that is the focus of the nutritional assessment study."}{"title": "TALL\u00cdMETRO:Tall\u00edmetro is a device used for measuring height, important in the assessment of nutritional status."}{"title": "B\u00c1SQUILA:B\u00e1squila refers to the scale used for measuring weight, which is essential in nutritional assessments."}{"title": "B\u00c1SICA:"}{"title": "SOCIEDAD DE NUTRICI\u00d3N Y DIET\u00c9TICA DE GALICIA:The Society of Nutrition and Dietetics of Galicia is an organization that focuses on nutritional assessment and guidelines in Galicia, Spain."}{"title": "M. POBLACI\u00d3N:Pastor M. Poblaci\u00f3n is a professional involved in geriatric nutritional assessment and standards."}{"title": "ALASTR\u00daE:Alastru\u00e9 is a reference for nutritional standards in Spain, particularly for the elderly population."}{"title": "ESQUIUS:Esquius is another reference for nutritional standards in Spain, specifically including elderly populations."}{"title": "X CONGRESO DE LA SOCIEDAD DE NUTRICI\u00d3N Y DIET\u00c9TICA DE GALICIA:The X Congress of the Society of Nutrition and Dietetics of Galicia held in La Coru\u00f1a in May 2000 focused on nutritional assessment for bedridden patients."}{"title": "SOCIETY OF NUTRITION AND DIETETICS OF GALICIA:"}{"title": "GERIATRIC NUTRITIONAL ASSESSMENT:Geriatric nutritional assessment focuses on evaluating the nutritional needs and status of elderly patients, ensuring they receive appropriate care."}{"title": "CIRCUNFERENCIA DEL BRAZO:The \"CIRCUNFERENCIA DEL BRAZO\" refers to a measurement utilized in nutritional assessment to evaluate muscle mass and overall nutritional status. This measurement is taken at the midpoint of the non-dominant arm, serving as an important indicator for assessing body composition."}{"title": "CIRCUNFERENCIA MUSCULAR DEL BRAZO:The \"CIRCUNFERENCIA MUSCULAR DEL BRAZO\" is a measurement used to assess the muscle mass of individuals, particularly in the context of nutritional evaluations. This measurement is significant as it can indicate changes in muscle mass, which may decrease in cases of malnutrition. Thus, the circumferential measurement of the arm serves as an important tool in evaluating an individual's nutritional status and overall health."}{"title": "PROTE\u00cdNAS PLASM\u00c1TICAS:\"PROTE\u00cdNAS PLASM\u00c1TICAS\" se refiere a las prote\u00ednas presentes en el plasma sangu\u00edneo, cuya concentraci\u00f3n es un indicador clave del estado del compartimento proteico visceral. Estas prote\u00ednas son fundamentales en la evaluaci\u00f3n nutricional, ya que se miden durante las valoraciones nutricionales para determinar el estado nutricional de los pacientes."}{"title": "RBP:RBP, or retinol-binding protein, is a crucial protein that plays a significant role in the transport of vitamin A within the body. It binds to retinol, which is essential for nutritional assessment and overall health. RBP is characterized by its short half-life, indicating that it is rapidly metabolized in the body. This protein is vital for maintaining adequate levels of vitamin A, which is important for various physiological functions, including vision, immune response, and cellular communication."}{"title": "CARDONA:Cardona is a method used for nutritional assessment in hospitalized patients."}{"title": "UL\u00cdBARRI:Ul\u00edbarri is an automated method for assessing nutritional risk."}{"title": "CHANG:Chang is a diagnostic test for assessing nutritional status."}{"title": "DYNAMOMETRY:Dynamometry is a method used to measure muscle strength, often employed in nutritional assessments."}{"title": "ISOTOPIC DILUTION TECHNIQUES:Isotopic dilution techniques are methods used to assess body composition and nutritional status."}{"title": "BIOELECTRICAL IMPEDANCE:Bioelectrical impedance is a method and technique utilized to assess body composition and nutritional status. It is particularly effective in evaluating body composition in malnourished patients, providing valuable insights into their nutritional health."}{"title": "ALIANZA M\u00c1SNUTRIDOS:Alianza M\u00e1snutridos is a coalition in Spain dedicated to tackling malnutrition associated with disease through a multidisciplinary approach. The organization focuses on implementing screening processes at various levels of healthcare to identify and address malnutrition effectively. Additionally, Alianza M\u00e1snutridos aims to raise awareness and integrate the issue of malnutrition into national and regional health strategies, ensuring that it is recognized as a critical component of public health initiatives."}{"title": "SOCIEDAD ESPA\u00d1OLA DE NUTRICI\u00d3N ENTERAL Y PARENTERAL:The \"Sociedad Espa\u00f1ola de Nutrici\u00f3n Enteral y Parenteral\" (SENPE) is a professional organization dedicated to the promotion and development of enteral and parenteral nutrition in Spain. It focuses on providing resources and support for clinical nutrition, particularly for patients with specific needs such as renal insufficiency and those undergoing hemodialysis. SENPE publishes guidelines and studies that address various aspects of nutritional support, including the administration and absorption of medications in patients receiving enteral nutrition. Through its efforts, SENPE aims to enhance the quality of nutritional care and ensure that healthcare professionals have access to the latest information and best practices in the field of enteral and parenteral nutrition."}{"title": "CONSEJO DE EUROPA:The Consejo de Europa is an international organization dedicated to promoting human rights, democracy, and the rule of law across Europe. In 2003, the Consejo de Europa issued recommendations specifically addressing the issue of hospital malnutrition, which included the establishment of guidelines aimed at guiding future actions in this critical area."}{"title": "HOLANDA:Holland has successfully implemented programs to combat malnutrition since 2007, aiming to gradually reduce its prevalence across all healthcare levels."}{"title": "NUTRITION DAY:Nutrition Day is an initiative organized by ESPEN that focuses on evaluating the nutrition of patients admitted to hospitals in order to assess the prevalence of malnutrition. This initiative aims to raise awareness and address the issue of malnutrition across Europe, highlighting its significance in healthcare settings."}{"title": "CONSEJO GENERAL DE ENFERMER\u00cdA:The Consejo General de Enfermer\u00eda is the governing body for nursing professionals in Spain, promoting nursing standards and practices."}{"title": "ALIANZA GENERAL DE PACIENTES:The Alianza General de Pacientes is an organization in Spain that represents patient interests and advocates for their rights in healthcare."}{"title": "SOCIEDAD ESPA\u00d1OLA DE MEDICINA DE FAMILIA Y COMUNITARIA:The Sociedad Espa\u00f1ola de Medicina de Familia y Comunitaria (semFYC) is a professional society for family medicine practitioners in Spain."}{"title": "SOCIEDAD ESPA\u00d1OLA DE M\u00c9DICOS DE ATENCI\u00d3N PRIMARIA:The Sociedad Espa\u00f1ola de M\u00e9dicos de Atenci\u00f3n Primaria (SEMERGEN) is an organization focused on the interests and education of primary care physicians in Spain."}{"title": "SOCIEDAD ESPA\u00d1OLA DE GASTROENTEROLOG\u00cdA, HEPATOLOG\u00cdA Y NUTRICI\u00d3N PEDI\u00c1TRICA:The Sociedad Espa\u00f1ola de Gastroenterolog\u00eda, Hepatolog\u00eda y Nutrici\u00f3n Pedi\u00e1trica (SGHNP) is a professional society dedicated to pediatric gastroenterology and nutrition in Spain."}{"title": "SOCIEDAD ESPA\u00d1OLA DE ONCOLOG\u00cdA RADIOTER\u00c1PICA:The Sociedad Espa\u00f1ola de Oncolog\u00eda Radioter\u00e1pica (SEOR) is an organization focused on the field of radiation oncology in Spain."}{"title": "FUNDACI\u00d3N ABBOTT:Fundaci\u00f3n Abbott is a foundation that supports health and nutrition initiatives, particularly in relation to malnutrition."}{"title": "SOCIEDAD ESPA\u00d1OLA DE DIRECTIVOS DE SALUD:The Sociedad Espa\u00f1ola de Directivos de Salud (SEDISA) is an organization representing health executives and managers in Spain."}{"title": "CONSEJO GENERAL DE COLEGIOS OFICIALES DE FARMAC\u00c9UTICOS:"}{"title": "SOCIEDAD ESPA\u00d1OLA DE ONCOLOG\u00cdA RADIOTERAP\u00c9TICA:"}{"title": "HOLAND\u00c9S:El Ministerio de Sanidad holand\u00e9s ha estado involucrado en la lucha contra la desnutrici\u00f3n en el pa\u00eds desde 2007."}{"title": "COSTE DE HOSPITALIZACI\u00d3N:El coste de hospitalizaci\u00f3n es un factor importante en la evaluaci\u00f3n de la desnutrici\u00f3n, ya que los pacientes desnutridos generan un gasto adicional diario."}{"title": "BRAUN:Braun is a company recognized for its innovative contributions to health and personal care, particularly through the development of nutritional assessment tools. Additionally, Braun is a manufacturer that specializes in producing nutritional solutions, which encompass a range of products, including parenteral nutrition offerings. This dual focus on both assessment and nutritional solutions highlights Braun's commitment to enhancing health and well-being through advanced technology and quality products."}{"title": "BURGOS PEL\u00c1EZ R:Burgos Pel\u00e1ez R is an author who contributed to the literature on malnutrition and disease."}{"title": "SULLIVAN DH:Sullivan DH is an author who studied the impact of nutrition status on morbidity and mortality in geriatric patients."}{"title": "VANITALLIE TB:Vanitallie TB is an author who has researched frailty in the elderly and its relation to nutrition."}{"title": "AGARWAL N:Agarwal N is an author who investigated the predictive ability of nutritional variables for mortality in elderly people."}{"title": "P\u00c9REZ DE LA CRUZ A:P\u00e9rez de la Cruz A is an author who studied malnutrition in hospitalized patients."}{"title": "CAMBRIDGE, UK:Cambridge, UK is the location of Cabi Publishing, which published works on disease-related malnutrition."}{"title": "COLLABORATIVE GROUP FOR THE STUDY OF HOSPITAL MALNUTRITION IN GALICIA:A group focused on studying hospital malnutrition in Galicia, Spain, and conducting nutritional status studies of inpatients."}{"title": "NUTRITIONDAY:An international event aimed at raising awareness about nutrition and malnutrition."}{"title": "FIGHT AGAINST MALNUTRITION:An initiative aimed at combating malnutrition through various strategies and awareness campaigns."}{"title": "NUTRITIONAL STATUS STUDY OF INPATIENTS IN HOSPITALS OF GALICIA:A study conducted to assess the nutritional status of inpatients in hospitals across Galicia, Spain."}{"title": "J NUTRITION HEALTH AGING:A journal that publishes research related to nutrition and health in aging populations."}{"title": "NUTR BURBANK LOS ANGEL CTY CALIF:A publication that discusses various aspects of nutrition, including screening and assessment tools."}{"title": "HOSPITAL UNIVERSITARIO VIRGEN DE LA VICTORIA:Hospital Universitario Virgen de la Victoria is a hospital situated in M\u00e1laga, Spain. It is known for conducting research in the fields of endocrinology and nutrition."}{"title": "VALORACI\u00d3N DE LA INGESTA:Assessment of intake refers to the evaluation of dietary habits and nutrient intake of individuals or populations."}{"title": "ELMADFA & MEYER:Elmadfa & Meyer are researchers who contributed to the study of population dietary intake and public health policy recommendations in 2014."}{"title": "WILLETT WC.:Willett WC. is a researcher known for studying food intake and its implications on nutritional status since 1998."}{"title": "SURVEY METHODS:Survey methods are tools used to estimate dietary intake at individual or collective levels, crucial for nutritional studies."}{"title": "NUTRITIONAL EDUCATION:Nutritional education is essential for successful dietary interventions and improving patient outcomes."}{"title": "ENCUESTAS DIET\u00c9TICAS:Encuestas diet\u00e9ticas are methods and surveys utilized to collect data on dietary intake, serving both individual and collective assessments. These surveys are essential for evaluating dietary habits and the nutritional intake of patients, playing a crucial role in managing nutritional health."}{"title": "ENCUESTAS NUTRICIONALES:Encuestas nutricionales are methods used to assess dietary intake and nutritional status of individuals or populations."}{"title": "SERIA MAJEM LL:Serra Majem Ll is an author referenced in the context of nutritional epidemiology and survey methods."}{"title": "RECORDATORIO DE 24 HORAS:The \"RECORDATORIO DE 24 HORAS\" is a dietary assessment tool utilized to evaluate an individual's food intake, which is particularly important for managing obesity. This method involves individuals recalling all foods and beverages they have consumed over the past 24 hours. It serves as a retrospective dietary assessment technique that quantifies food and beverage intake, providing valuable insights into dietary habits and nutritional status."}{"title": "CUESTIONARIO DE FRECUENCIA DE CONSUMO:The \"Cuestionario de Frecuencia de Consumo\" is a survey method designed to evaluate how frequently specific foods are consumed within a defined time frame. It serves as a predefined questionnaire that assesses habitual food intake, allowing for a comprehensive analysis of dietary patterns. This tool is instrumental in measuring dietary intake over a specified period, providing valuable insights into individuals' eating habits."}{"title": "ENCUESTAS FAMILIARES:Encuestas familiares are surveys conducted to gather dietary information from households."}{"title": "HOJAS DE BALANCE ALIMENTARIO:Hojas de balance alimentario are tools used to assess food supply and consumption in a population."}{"title": "REGISTRO DIET\u00c9TICO:"}{"title": "ARANCETA B:Aranceta B is an author referenced in the document, contributing to the discussion on dietary assessment methods."}{"title": "REGISTRO/DIARIO DIET\u00c9TICO:The Registro/Diario Diet\u00e9tico is a method for recording food and beverage intake over a specified period, often used in dietary assessments."}{"title": "M\u00c9TODOS DE EVALUACI\u00d3N DE LA INGESTA DE ALIMENTOS:This refers to various methods for assessing food intake, including the 24-hour recall, dietary records, and food frequency questionnaires."}{"title": "PUNTO CLAVE:A key point in determining the type of questionnaire to be used based on available resources and interviewer capabilities."}{"title": "M\u00c9TODO DE VALORACI\u00d3N DE LA INGESTA:A method for assessing dietary intake, which can be useful if preceded by careful design and planning."}{"title": "LIMITACIONES:Refers to the limitations associated with different dietary assessment methods that need to be considered."}{"title": "CUESTIONARIO ABIERTO-CERRADO:A type of questionnaire format that can be used in dietary assessments."}{"title": "ENTREVISTADOR:Refers to the interviewer who may administer certain dietary assessment methods."}{"title": "AUTADMINISTRADO:Refers to self-administered questionnaires that can be used in dietary assessments."}{"title": "SUBJETIVO:Refers to the subjective nature of certain dietary assessment methods."}{"title": "COSTE:COSTE refers to the financial expenditure associated with healthcare interventions, which is a critical factor in analyses of cost-effectiveness and cost-utility. Additionally, COSTE encompasses the costs associated with various dietary assessment methods. This dual focus highlights the importance of understanding both healthcare and dietary costs in evaluating overall health interventions and their economic implications."}{"title": "COOPERACI\u00d3N:Refers to the level of cooperation required from participants in dietary assessments."}{"title": "RECURSOS DISPONIBLES:"}{"title": "IENVA:IENVA is an online platform and organization dedicated to providing individuals with tools for nutritional analysis and dietary record-keeping. It offers access to comprehensive food composition databases and nutritional information, enabling users to track their food intake and understand the nutritional composition of their meals. Additionally, IENVA features a food composition table and a nutritional analysis program that includes detailed reporting, making it a valuable resource for those looking to manage their diet effectively."}{"title": "HERN\u00c1NDEZ:Hern\u00e1ndez is a researcher noted for contributions to the study of dietary intake methods, with a particular focus on the 24-hour recall method. Additionally, Hern\u00e1ndez (2010) is referenced in the text concerning the food consumption frequency questionnaire, indicating the relevance of their work in the field of dietary assessment and nutrition research."}{"title": "GIBSON:Gibson is a researcher who has studied dietary assessment methods, including the use of household measures and food models in dietary recalls."}{"title": "CUESTIONARIO DE FRECUENCIA DE CONSUMO DE ALIMENTOS:A questionnaire designed to gather data on food consumption frequency over a specific time period, including variations by season and special occasions."}{"title": "SHIM ET AL.:Shim et al. are researchers noted for their contributions to dietary assessment methodologies. In their 2014 study, they highlighted the effectiveness of the 24-hour recall method for evaluating dietary intake. Additionally, they provided valuable insights into the administration of dietary questionnaires, further enhancing the understanding of dietary assessment techniques."}{"title": "MARGETTS & NELSON:Margetts & Nelson (1997) is a reference cited in discussions regarding the limitations of dietary assessment methods. They are recognized as researchers who have made significant contributions to the methodology of dietary assessment, enhancing the understanding and application of these methods in nutritional research."}{"title": "HTTP://WWW.CHOOSEMYPLATE.GOV/:A website providing dietary guidelines and resources for healthy eating."}{"title": "HTTP://WWW.SEH-LELHA.ORG/CALENA.ASPX:A website offering tools and resources for dietary assessment and nutrition."}{"title": "HTTP://WWW.IENVA.ORG/CALCDIETA/:A website that provides dietary calculation tools and resources."}{"title": "HUEVOS, CARNES, PESCADOS:A category of food items that includes eggs, meats, and fish, which are part of the food frequency questionnaire."}{"title": "LECHE ENTERA:LECHE ENTERA, or whole milk, is a dairy product that is included in dietary plans and is also listed in food frequency questionnaires. It serves as a significant component in various nutritional guidelines, highlighting its importance in a balanced diet."}{"title": "LECHE SEMIDESNATADA:LECHE SEMIDESNATADA refers to semi-skimmed milk, which is a moderate-fat dairy product. It is commonly included in food frequency questionnaires, indicating its relevance in dietary assessments. This type of milk offers a balance between full-fat and skim milk, making it a popular choice for those seeking a lower fat option while still enjoying the taste and nutritional benefits of milk."}{"title": "LECHE DESCREMADA:Leche descremada, also known as skim milk, is a lower-fat milk option that is commonly consumed. It is a dairy product that is often included in food frequency questionnaires, highlighting its relevance in dietary assessments."}{"title": "LECHE CONDENSADA:Condensed milk, a dairy product listed in the food frequency questionnaire."}{"title": "NATA O CREMA DE LECHE:Cream, a dairy product listed in the food frequency questionnaire."}{"title": "BATIDOS DE LECHE:Milkshakes, a dairy product listed in the food frequency questionnaire."}{"title": "YOGURT ENTERO:Whole yogurt, a dairy product listed in the food frequency questionnaire."}{"title": "YOGURT DESCREMADO:Skimmed yogurt, a dairy product listed in the food frequency questionnaire."}{"title": "PETIT SUISSE:A type of soft cheese, listed in the food frequency questionnaire."}{"title": "REQUET\u00d3N O CUAJADA:Cottage cheese, a dairy product listed in the food frequency questionnaire."}{"title": "QUESO EN PORCIONES O CREMOSO:Portion cheese or creamy cheese, a dairy product listed in the food frequency questionnaire."}{"title": "QUESOS CURADOS, SEMICURADOS:Cured and semi-cured cheeses, listed in the food frequency questionnaire."}{"title": "QUESO BLANCO O FRESCO:Fresh cheese, a dairy product listed in the food frequency questionnaire."}{"title": "NATILLAS, FLAN, PUDING:Custards, flans, and puddings, listed in the food frequency questionnaire."}{"title": "HUEVOS DE GALLINA:Chicken eggs, listed in the food frequency questionnaire."}{"title": "POLLO O PAVO CON PIEL:Chicken or turkey with skin, listed in the food frequency questionnaire."}{"title": "POLLO O PAVO SIN PIEL:The entity \"POLLO O PAVO SIN PIEL\" refers to chicken or turkey that is prepared without skin. This option is included in the food frequency questionnaire, indicating its relevance in dietary assessments. Additionally, skinless chicken or turkey is permitted in modified diets, making it a suitable choice for individuals seeking healthier protein options."}{"title": "CARNE DE TERNERA O VACA:Beef, listed in the food frequency questionnaire."}{"title": "CARNE DE CERDO:Pork, listed in the food frequency questionnaire."}{"title": "CARNE DE CORDERO:CARNE DE CORDERO, or lamb, is a type of meat that is noted for its higher phosphorus content compared to other meats, which makes it less recommended for certain dietary considerations. Despite this, lamb is included in food frequency questionnaires, indicating its relevance in dietary assessments and consumption patterns."}{"title": "CONEJO O LIEBRE:Rabbit or hare, listed in the food frequency questionnaire."}{"title": "OTRAS V\u00cdSCERAS:Other organ meats, listed in the food frequency questionnaire.)<|COMPLETE|>"}{"title": "CFC:CFC is a method used for dietary assessment that does not modify the habits of the person surveyed and is relatively easy to develop."}{"title": "RIBEFOOD:Ribefood is an interactive web application designed for dietary adherence surveys."}{"title": "ENCUESTA DE ADHERENCIA A LA DIETA MEDITERR\u00c1NEA:The Encuesta de Adherencia a la Dieta Mediterr\u00e1nea is a survey designed to assess adherence to the Mediterranean diet."}{"title": "NUTRIENTE:NUTRIENTE refers to the nutrients that are investigated in dietary studies to understand their impact on health."}{"title": "DIETISTA-NUTRICIONISTA:A Dietitian-Nutritionist is a trained health professional specializing in nutrition and dietetics. They conduct dietary interviews to gather detailed information about individuals' eating habits and provide guidance on the appropriate intake of foods and liquids. In a clinical setting, a dietitian-nutritionist works under the supervision of a physician to manage dietary needs and meal planning, particularly in hospitals. Their role is essential in advising patients on how to maintain a balanced diet and make informed food choices to support their health."}{"title": "RED MEATS:Red meats are consumed less frequently in the Mediterranean diet, emphasizing lower intake for health benefits."}{"title": "DIETARY HISTORY:Dietary history refers to the process of assessing an individual's eating habits and fluid intake over time, with a particular focus on identifying foods that may contribute to health issues such as kidney stone formation. This method involves gathering detailed information about a patient's dietary practices, which can provide valuable insights for healthcare professionals in understanding and managing potential dietary-related health concerns."}{"title": "OLIVE OIL:"}{"title": "FORO ACT\u00daA:Foro Act\u00faa is a web resource that provides information and tools for modifying dietary habits, particularly for patients with overweight and obesity."}{"title": "MATAIX J:Mataix J is an author of a classic food composition table in the national context."}{"title": "MOREIRAS-VARELA O:Moreiras-Varela O is an author of a classic food composition table in the national context."}{"title": "AND\u00daJAR MM:And\u00fajar MM is an author of a classic food composition table in the national context."}{"title": "CSIC:The Spanish National Research Council (CSIC) is involved in the development of food composition tables."}{"title": "TABLAS DE COMPOSICI\u00d3N DE ALIMENTOS:TABLAS DE COMPOSICI\u00d3N DE ALIMENTOS, or Food Composition Tables, are comprehensive compilations of data that detail the nutritional composition of a wide variety of foods. These tables provide essential information regarding the nutritional content of foods, including specific nutrients such as phosphorus levels. They serve as a valuable resource for understanding the dietary contributions of different foods and are utilized in nutrition research, dietary planning, and food labeling."}{"title": "BASES DE DATOS DE ALIMENTOS:Food Databases are digital collections of nutritional information about food items."}{"title": "APLICACIONES M\u00d3VILES:Mobile Applications are software tools that provide nutritional information and dietary tracking for users."}{"title": "CUESTIONARIO DE H\u00c1BITOS:"}{"title": "UNITED STATES DEPARTMENT OF AGRICULTURE:The United States Department of Agriculture (USDA) is a government agency that provides comprehensive food composition databases, including nutritional information about various food items."}{"title": "DIETOWIN:DIETOWIN\u00ae is a nutritional analysis software developed by Biol\u00f3gica Tecnolog\u00eda M\u00e9dica, S.L. that helps in analyzing dietary intake and creating personalized diets."}{"title": "DIETSOURCE:DIETSOURCE\u00ae is a nutritional analysis program developed by Nestl\u00e9 Consumer Health, designed to assist in dietary assessments and planning. This user-friendly software is particularly beneficial for dietitians, providing them with the tools necessary to conduct thorough dietary evaluations and create effective nutrition plans."}{"title": "EASYDIET:EASYDIET\u00ae is a nutritional analysis tool that can be used for dietary assessments and personalized diet creation."}{"title": "NUTRITIONAL DATABASES:Nutritional databases are collections of data that provide information on the nutritional composition of various food items, used for dietary analysis and research."}{"title": "NUTRITIONAL ANALYSIS:Nutritional analysis is a process that evaluates the nutritional content of food items to ensure that products meet the initial nutritional proposal and comply with established nutritional ranges. This analysis often involves the use of software tools and databases to assess dietary intake, providing a comprehensive understanding of the nutritional value of various foods."}{"title": "NUTRITIONAL INFORMATION:Nutritional information includes data about the nutrients contained in food items, such as macronutrients, vitamins, and minerals, essential for dietary planning and health."}{"title": "NUTRITIONAL TOOLS:Nutritional tools are resources, including software and online platforms, that assist individuals and professionals in analyzing dietary intake and planning diets."}{"title": "DIETARY INTAKE:Dietary intake refers to the total amount of food and drink consumed by an individual, which is analyzed for nutritional content and health implications."}{"title": "NUTRITIONAL DATABASE:Nutritional databases are collections of data that provide information on the nutritional composition of various food items, used for dietary analysis and research.)<|COMPLETE|>"}{"title": "FORO ACTUA:FORO ACTUA is a web platform that offers interactive nutritional analysis, recipe analysis, and dietary habits surveys."}{"title": "MYFITNESSPAL:Myfitnesspal is a multi-format platform (web and apps) that provides an uncontrolled food table and exercise logging."}{"title": "DIETSTAT:DIETSTAT is a program used at Hospital Carlos Haya in M\u00e1laga for dietary analysis and patient intake assessment."}{"title": "NUTRISOL:NUTRISOL is a program from the Department of Preventive Medicine at the University of M\u00e1laga for nutritional analysis."}{"title": "MALAGA:M\u00e1laga is a city in Spain where the Hospital Carlos Haya is located, which utilizes the DIETSTAT program."}{"title": "KOREA:Korea is a country where the Diet Evaluation System (DES) was developed for standardized face-to-face dietary interviews."}{"title": "NIH:The National Institutes of Health (NIH) is an organization that has highlighted key points in the management of celiac disease. Additionally, the NIH is involved in developing projects focused on dietary evaluation technologies, indicating its commitment to advancing research and improving health outcomes related to dietary conditions."}{"title": "CAMEMBERT:Camembert is a soft cheese from France, also classified under Dairy and Egg Products, recognized for its rich flavor and creamy interior."}{"title": "CARAWAY CHEESE:Caraway cheese is a type of cheese flavored with caraway seeds, falling under the Dairy and Egg Products category."}{"title": "CHEDDAR:Cheddar is a popular hard cheese originating from England, known for its sharp taste and versatility in cooking, classified under Dairy and Egg Products."}{"title": "CHESHIRE CHEESE:Cheshire cheese is a traditional English cheese known for its crumbly texture and distinct flavor, categorized under Dairy and Egg Products."}{"title": "COLBY:Colby is a semi-hard cheese from the United States, recognized for its mild flavor and open texture, classified under Dairy and Egg Products."}{"title": "COTTAGE CHEESE:Cottage cheese is a fresh cheese curd product with a mild flavor, categorized under Dairy and Egg Products, often used in various dishes."}{"title": "CREAM CHEESE:Cream cheese is a soft, spreadable cheese made from milk and cream, classified under Dairy and Egg Products, commonly used in desserts and spreads."}{"title": "EDAM:Edam is a semi-hard cheese originating from the Netherlands, known for its mild flavor and red wax coating, categorized under Dairy and Egg Products."}{"title": "BRIE:"}{"title": "ROCHE:Roche is a pharmaceutical company involved in the development of the GoCARB Project, which is related to dietary assessment."}{"title": "GO CARB PROJECT:The GoCARB Project is an initiative by Roche aimed at improving dietary assessment methods."}{"title": "DIETARY DATA RECORD SYSTEM:The Dietary Data Record System (DDRS) is a project that integrates sensor technology for real-time recording of food intake."}{"title": "FOOD INTAKE RECORDING SOFTWARE SYSTEM:The Food Intake Recording Software System (FIRSST) is a project designed to assist in dietary assessment."}{"title": "IMPROVING DIETARY ASSESSMENT METHODS USING THE CELL PHONE AND DIGITAL IMAGING:This project focuses on enhancing dietary assessment methods through the use of mobile technology and digital imaging."}{"title": "AUTOMATED SELF-ASSISTED 24-HOUR DIETARY RECALL:The Automated Self-Assisted 24-h Dietary Recall (ASA24) is a system that helps individuals recall their dietary intake over a 24-hour period."}{"title": "MOBILE FOOD INTAKE VISUALIZATION AND VOICE RECOGNIZER:The Mobile Food Intake Visualization and Voice Recognizer (FIVR) is a project aimed at improving dietary assessment through mobile technology."}{"title": "REGISTER DIET\u00c9TICO FOTOGR\u00c1FICO:The Registro Diet\u00e9tico Fotogr\u00e1fico (RDF) is a method of dietary assessment that uses photographic records of food intake."}{"title": "ARAB ET AL.:Arab et al. is a reference to researchers who have worked on dietary assessment methods using images."}{"title": "GREGORY ET AL.:Gregory et al. is a reference to researchers involved in the development of dietary assessment technologies."}{"title": "KIKUNAGA ET AL.:Kikunaga et al. is a reference to researchers who have contributed to the field of dietary assessment."}{"title": "PORCA ET AL.:Porca et al. is a reference to researchers who have studied the impact of technology on dietary assessment."}{"title": "GEMMING ET AL.:"}{"title": "NUEVAS TECNOLOG\u00cdAS:Nuevas tecnolog\u00edas refer to the advancements in technology that facilitate the assessment and management of dietary intake in clinical practice."}{"title": "PATOLOG\u00cdA METAB\u00d3LICA Y NUTRICIONAL:Patolog\u00eda metab\u00f3lica y nutricional encompasses various health conditions related to diet and nutrition that require clinical management."}{"title": "GIBSON RS:Gibson RS is an author and expert in nutritional assessment, particularly in measuring food consumption."}{"title": "M\u00c9TODOS NUTRICIONALES:M\u00e9todos nutricionales are techniques and approaches used to assess and improve dietary habits and nutritional health."}{"title": "RECURSOS INFORM\u00c1TICOS:Recursos inform\u00e1ticos are technological tools and resources that support dietary assessment and clinical practice."}{"title": "EVALUACI\u00d3N DE LA INGESTA:"}{"title": "COMPLEJO HOSPITALARIO DE NAVARRA:The Complejo Hospitalario de Navarra is a hospital located in Pamplona, responsible for providing clinical nutrition and dietetic services."}{"title": "DIETA HOSPITALARIA:\"DIETA HOSPITALARIA\" refers to a structured dietary plan specifically designed for patients in a hospital setting. This dietary protocol is crucial for patient recovery and management, as it focuses on meeting the nutritional needs and restrictions based on individual medical conditions. The planning of hospital diets involves careful consideration of various dietary restrictions and guidelines to ensure that patients receive proper nutrition, which is essential for their health management and overall recovery."}{"title": "SECCI\u00d3N NUTRICI\u00d3N CL\u00cdNICA Y DIET\u00c9TICA:The Clinical Nutrition and Dietetics section is responsible for planning and managing dietary needs in the hospital."}{"title": "COCINA:Cocina refers to the kitchen facilities in a hospital, which play a crucial role in meal preparation and service for patients."}{"title": "T\u00c9CNICO SUPERIOR EN DIET\u00c9TICA:A professional responsible for planning and calibrating dietary menus in a hospital setting, ensuring nutritional quality."}{"title": "PROGRAMAS INFORM\u00c1TICOS:Software systems used in hospitals to manage dietary requests and meal planning efficiently."}{"title": "C\u00c1MARAS FRIGOR\u00cdFICAS:Refrigeration units in hospitals that store prepared meals at safe temperatures to ensure food safety."}{"title": "MEN\u00daS:Menus are the planned lists of meals provided to patients, tailored to their dietary needs."}{"title": "SECCI\u00d3N DE ALIMENTACI\u00d3N:A department within the hospital that collaborates with dietitians to ensure meal quality."}{"title": "PERSONAL DE ENFERMER\u00cdA:The \"Personal de Enfermer\u00eda\" refers to the nursing staff responsible for various critical functions in patient care. This group includes both nurses and nursing assistants who are tasked with placing catheters and managing venous access in patients. Additionally, they play a vital role in translating dietary guidelines and monitoring patient intake within hospital settings. Their responsibilities encompass both technical procedures and patient education, ensuring comprehensive care for individuals under their supervision."}{"title": "M\u00c9DICOS:M\u00e9dicos are doctors who assess patients' nutritional status and collaborate with the Unidad de Nutrici\u00f3n for dietary needs."}{"title": "RESOLUCI\u00d3N RES AP (2003) 3:A resolution by the Council of Europe regarding food and nutritional care in hospitals, establishing recommendations for improving patient care."}{"title": "REGLAMENTO 1169/2011:A regulation in the European Union that sets legal standards for food information to consumers, including nutritional labeling in collective dining settings like hospitals."}{"title": "ISO 22000:2005:ISO 22000:2005 is an international standard that ensures food safety based on the APPCC system and is similar in structure to ISO 9000."}{"title": "GU\u00cdA DE PR\u00c1CTICAS CORRECTAS DE HIGIENE Y MANIPULACI\u00d3N:A document that outlines the fundamental hygiene requirements for food operations to ensure food safety."}{"title": "AN\u00c1LISIS MICROBIOL\u00d3GICOS:Microbiological analyses conducted periodically on food and surfaces in hospitals to ensure safety and hygiene."}{"title": "SEGURIDAD ALIMENTARIA:Food safety practices aimed at preventing foodborne illnesses and ensuring the health of consumers, particularly in hospital settings."}{"title": "PERSONAL DE COCINA:Kitchen staff responsible for food preparation and ensuring hygiene standards are met in hospital kitchens."}{"title": "TOXIINFECCIONES ALIMENTARIAS:"}{"title": "HOSPITAL DIET:The \"HOSPITAL DIET\" encompasses a systematic approach to diet planning for hospitalized patients, focusing on their unique physiological and pathological conditions. It involves the selection of appropriate dietary plans that cater to the specific health needs of patients, particularly after surgeries such as bariatric surgery. Hospital diets are structured meal plans designed to effectively manage nutritional intake, especially for individuals with specific health conditions like diabetes. These nutritional plans and protocols are established to ensure that patients receive the necessary dietary support during their hospital stay, taking into account their dietary restrictions and health requirements."}{"title": "DIETAS PROGRESIVAS:\"DIETAS PROGRESIVAS\" refers to a series of dietary plans specifically designed to support recovery and adapt to changes in a patient's condition following surgery or during medical treatment. These progressive diets are utilized to aid in the restoration of digestive function after a period of fasting, ensuring that patients can gradually reintroduce food in a manner that is safe and conducive to their healing process."}{"title": "DIETAS ESPECIALES:Special diets are non-coded diets tailored to individual patient needs."}{"title": "NUTRIENT DISTRIBUTION:Nutrient distribution in hospital diets typically consists of 50-55% carbohydrates, 30-35% lipids, and 10-20% proteins."}{"title": "DIETARY RESTRICTIONS:Dietary restrictions are essential for managing the health of patients with adrenoleucodistrofia, primarily aimed at limiting the intake of very long-chain fatty acids. In addition to this specific restriction, dietary guidelines for these patients may also encompass a variety of other limitations, including gluten-free, low-purine, and vegetarian options. These comprehensive dietary restrictions are designed to support the overall well-being and nutritional needs of individuals affected by this condition."}{"title": "ODONTOLOGICAL/FA\u0301CIL MASTICACI\u00d3N:Odontological/easy chewing diets are tailored for patients with chewing or swallowing difficulties."}{"title": "HIPERPROTEICA:HIPERPROTEICA refers to a high-protein diet specifically designed for patients who require an increased protein intake. This includes individuals suffering from conditions such as burns or those experiencing metabolic stress, where the body\u2019s protein needs are elevated. The Hiperproteica diet is particularly beneficial for patients with burns or increased catabolism, as it helps support recovery and maintain muscle mass during periods of heightened protein demand."}{"title": "DIAB\u00c9TICA NI\u00d1OS PEQUE\u00d1OS:Diabetic diets for small children are designed for children under 6 years with diabetes."}{"title": "DIAB\u00c9TICA NI\u00d1OS GRANDES:Diabetic diets for older children are tailored for children over 6 years with diabetes."}{"title": "CEL\u00cdACA:Cel\u00edaca diets are gluten-free diets for patients with gluten intolerance."}{"title": "POBRE EN COLESTEROL:Pobre en colesterol diets are low-cholesterol diets aimed at patients with dyslipidemia."}{"title": "LAXANTE:Laxante diets are designed for patients suffering from constipation."}{"title": "NO CARNE:No carne diets are for patients with meat intolerance."}{"title": "F\u00c1CIL DIGESTI\u00d3N:"}{"title": "LUNES:Lunes is the Spanish word for Monday, representing the first day of the week in the diet plan."}{"title": "MARTES:Martes is the Spanish word for Tuesday, representing the second day of the week in the diet plan."}{"title": "MI\u00c9RCOLES:Mi\u00e9rcoles is the Spanish word for Wednesday, representing the third day of the week in the diet plan."}{"title": "JUEVES:Jueves is the Spanish word for Thursday, representing the fourth day of the week in the diet plan."}{"title": "VIERNES:Viernes is the Spanish word for Friday, representing the fifth day of the week in the diet plan."}{"title": "S\u00c1BADO:S\u00e1bado is the Spanish word for Saturday, representing the sixth day of the week in the diet plan."}{"title": "DOMINGO:Domingo is the Spanish word for Sunday, representing the seventh day of the week in the diet plan."}{"title": "LECHE DESNATADA:Leche Desnatada is skim milk, a low-fat dairy product included in the diet plan for breakfast."}{"title": "BOLLER\u00cdA:Boller\u00eda refers to a variety of baked goods, commonly known as pastries, which are often included in breakfast options within certain diet plans. These baked goods may contain high levels of fructose and sorbitol, which can affect individuals with specific intolerances. While some pastries can vary in gluten content, making them potentially suitable for gluten-free diets, it is important to note that pastries are not permitted in modified diets. Dietary guidelines suggest that pastries should be consumed occasionally and in moderation."}{"title": "LENTEJAS ESTOFADAS:Lentejas Estofadas are a nutritious dish made from stewed lentils, often served as a first course in various diet plans. This dish is particularly notable for its high fiber content, making it a suitable option for those following a laxative diet. The combination of lentils provides not only essential nutrients but also promotes digestive health, aligning with dietary recommendations for increased fiber intake."}{"title": "FIDEOS A LA CAZUELA:Fideos a la cazuela are noodles cooked in a casserole style, served as a first course."}{"title": "POTAJE DE GARBANZOS:Potaje de Garbanzos is a chickpea stew that serves as a nutritious first course option in various diet plans. This dish is particularly notable for its inclusion in the laxative diet, as it is made with chickpeas, which are high in fiber. The high fiber content of chickpeas contributes to digestive health, making Potaje de Garbanzos a beneficial choice for those seeking to improve their dietary habits."}{"title": "ARROZ CON MEJILLONES Y CALAMAR:Arroz con Mejillones y Calamar is rice with mussels and squid, served as a first course."}{"title": "BERZA CON PATATAS:Berza con Patatas is a dish made of greens and potatoes, included in the first course options."}{"title": "GUISANTES PRIMAVERA:Guisantes Primavera refers to spring peas that are typically served as a first course. This dish is notable for its inclusion in a laxative diet, as it is made with spring peas that are high in fiber. The combination of these characteristics highlights Guisantes Primavera as both a flavorful and health-conscious option."}{"title": "ESPAGUETIS BOLO\u00d1ESA:Espaguetis Bolo\u00f1esa are spaghetti served with a Bolognese sauce, included in the first course options."}{"title": "ENSALADA DE LA TIERRA:Ensalada de la Tierra is a salad made with local ingredients, served as a first course."}{"title": "ALUBIA VERDES CON PATATA:Alubia Verdes con Patata is a dish of green beans with potatoes, served as a first course."}{"title": "ENSALADA MIXTA:Ensalada Mixta is a mixed salad, included in the first course options."}{"title": "CARDOS A LA NAVARRA:Cardos a la Navarra is a dish that features cardoon, a vegetable known for its high fiber content, making it suitable for a laxative diet. This dish is typically served as a first course, highlighting the unique flavor and texture of the cardoon."}{"title": "POCHAS CON VERDURAS:Pochas con Verduras is a gluten-free dish that consists of beans and vegetables. It is part of the gluten-free meal plan and is included in the first course options. Additionally, Pochas con Verduras is recognized as a dish suitable for a laxative diet, as it provides dietary fiber, making it beneficial for digestive health."}{"title": "PATATAS A LA RIOJANA:Patatas a la Riojana is a dish of potatoes prepared in the style of La Rioja, served as a first course."}{"title": "BORRAJA CON PATATAS:Borraja con Patatas is a dish made with borage and potatoes, included in the first course options."}{"title": "FRUTA:FRUTA refers to a variety of fruits that are included in dietary plans, specifically noted to exclude bananas. These fruits serve as a dessert option within the diet plan and are often incorporated into meals and snacks due to their nutritional benefits and natural sweetness."}{"title": "YOGUR:Yogur is a dairy product that is recognized for its numerous health benefits and dietary versatility. It is a food item that is often included in a moderate low-sodium diet and serves as a dessert option in various meal plans. Yogur undergoes fermentation, a process that involves bacteria that help to partially hydrolyze lactose, making it more tolerable for individuals who are lactose intolerant. This fermentation process not only improves lactose digestion but also enhances the overall nutritional profile of the yogurt.\n\nYogur contains 2.2 mg of iron per 100 grams and has a glycemic index of 51, indicating its moderate impact on blood sugar levels. It is also a good source of calcium, which is essential for bone health, and is recommended for daily intake. Additionally, yogur is beneficial for gut health, particularly during episodes of diarrhea, as it contains probiotics that support digestive function.\n\nFurthermore, yogur is a soft food option suitable for patients with dysphagia, although caution is advised when mixing it with fruits due to potential risks. Overall, yogur is a nutritious and versatile food that can be enjoyed by a wide range of individuals, contributing positively to their dietary needs."}{"title": "NATILLAS:Natillas are a type of custard-like dessert that is included in various dessert options. This dessert may contain ingredients that some individuals with dietary restrictions need to avoid, making it important for those with specific dietary needs to check the ingredients before consumption."}{"title": "ARROZ CON LECHE:Arroz con Leche is rice pudding, served as a dessert option."}{"title": "HELADO:Helado is ice cream, included in the dessert options."}{"title": "FLAN:FLAN is a type of caramel custard dessert that is commonly served as a dessert option. However, it may contain ingredients that some individuals with dietary restrictions need to avoid."}{"title": "CUAJADA:Cuajada is a gluten-free curd dessert that is included in the low-purine diet. It is recognized as a type of curd dessert and is featured among the dessert options available."}{"title": "LECHE CON DESCAFEINADO:Leche con Descafeinado is decaffeinated milk, served as a snack option."}{"title": "ENSALADA DE ARROZ:Ensalada de Arroz is a rice salad, served as a first course for dinner."}{"title": "CREMA DE ESP\u00c1RRAGOS:Crema de Esp\u00e1rragos is asparagus cream soup, included in the first course options for dinner."}{"title": "SOPA DE PESCADO:Sopa de Pescado is fish soup, served as a first course for dinner."}{"title": "PUR\u00c9 DE PATATAS Y ZANAHORIA:Pur\u00e9e de Patatas y Zanahoria is a mashed potato and carrot dish, included in the first course options for dinner."}{"title": "ENSALADA CAMPERA:\"ENSALADA CAMPERA\" is a gluten-free country-style salad that is included in gluten-free diets and various dietary plans. This rustic salad is typically served as a first course for dinner, highlighting its role as a wholesome and versatile dish suitable for those seeking gluten-free options."}{"title": "MENESTRA SALTEADA CON JAM\u00d3N:Menestra Salteada con Jam\u00f3n is saut\u00e9ed vegetables with ham, included in the first course options for dinner."}{"title": "JUD\u00cdAS VERDES CON TOMATE:Jud\u00edas Verdes con Tomate is green beans with tomato, served as a first course for dinner."}{"title": "FOGONERO ANDALUZA:Fogonero Andaluza is a dish from Andalusia, served as a second course for dinner."}{"title": "EMPANADILLAS DE BONITO:Empanadillas de Bonito are small tuna pastries, included in the second course options for dinner."}{"title": "TORTILLA DE JAM\u00d3N:Tortilla de Jam\u00f3n is a ham omelet that is included in dietary recommendations and is typically served as a second course for dinner."}{"title": "PLATIJA ROMANA:PlatiJa Romana is a Roman-style flatfish dish, included in the second course options for dinner."}{"title": "AT\u00daN ENCEBOLLADO:At\u00fan Encebollado is tuna cooked with onions, served with rice pilaf as a second course."}{"title": "PECHUGA VILLAROY:Pechuga Villaroy is a breaded chicken breast dish, included in the second course options for dinner."}{"title": "JAM\u00d3N AL HORNO:Jamon al Horno is baked ham, served with broccoli and carrots as a second course."}{"title": "HUEVOS GRAT\u00c9N:Huevos Graten are baked eggs, included in the second course options for dinner."}{"title": "FILETE DE ABADEJO:Filete de Abadejo is a fillet of coley fish, served with carrots as a second course."}{"title": "RAPE EN SALSA MARINERA:Rape en Salsa Marinera is monkfish in a marinara sauce, included in the second course options for dinner."}{"title": "SALCHICHAS AL VINO:Salchichas al V(\"entity\""}{"title": "TORTILLA DE CALABAC\u00cdN:Tortilla de Calabac\u00edn is a gluten-free zucchini omelet that is part of the gluten-free meal plan and included in dietary recommendations. This dish serves as a nutritious option within the second course selections for dinner, highlighting its versatility and suitability for those seeking gluten-free meal choices."}{"title": "LENGUADO A LA MENI\u00c8RE:Lenguado a la Meni\u00e8re is sole fish prepared in a classic French style, served as a second course."}{"title": "HUEVOS EN SALSA:Huevos en Salsa are eggs served in a sauce, included in the second course options for dinner."}{"title": "DIETA SEMIL\u00cdQUIDA:The \"DIETA SEMIL\u00cdQUIDA\" is recognized as the second step in dietary progression. It consists of a combination of liquid and pasty foods, which are designed to stimulate digestion more effectively than a strictly liquid diet. This dietary approach serves as a transitional phase, allowing individuals to gradually reintroduce more solid foods while still maintaining a focus on easily digestible options."}{"title": "DIETA SEMIBLANDA:The \"DIETA SEMIBLANDA\" is a dietary phase that follows the semiliquid diet, characterized by the inclusion of soft foods that are easier to chew and digest. This diet serves as a transitional step in the progression of dietary intake, introducing solid foods while assessing the individual's tolerance to protein and encouraging the process of chewing."}{"title": "DIETA BLANDA:\"Dieta blanda\" is a dietary phase characterized by the inclusion of soft foods that are easy to digest, making it particularly suitable for patients recovering from surgery. It serves as a progression from the semi-soft diet and is indicated for individuals experiencing digestive alterations. This diet encompasses a variety of solid textures, ensuring that it meets the nutritional needs of those who may have difficulty with more complex foods."}{"title": "GALLETAS:Galletas, commonly known as cookies, are a type of baked good that can vary significantly in their gluten content. While some galletas may be suitable for gluten-free diets, many traditional varieties contain gluten, making them unsuitable for individuals with celiac disease. Galletas are often consumed as a snack, providing enjoyment and energy, and they are included in various dietary recommendations. Nutritionally, galletas contain approximately 2 mg of iron per 100 grams. However, it is important to note that some galletas can be hard and may fragment easily, which poses risks for patients with dysphagia, a condition that affects swallowing. Overall, galletas are a versatile snack option, but considerations regarding gluten content and texture are essential for certain dietary needs."}{"title": "MERENDA:Merienda is a light meal or snack typically consumed in the afternoon. It often includes items such as galletas (cookies) and leche (milk). This tradition emphasizes a casual and enjoyable break during the day, allowing individuals to recharge with simple yet satisfying food options."}{"title": "DESAYUNO:Desayuno refers to breakfast, the first meal of the day, which is essential for providing the necessary energy and nutrients to start the day. This meal can include a variety of specific items tailored for dietary management and restrictions, making it suitable for patients with particular health needs. Common components of a traditional desayuno may include leche (milk), pan (bread), and mermelada (jam), as well as other foods such as dairy products, cereals, and fruit. These items are important for meeting nutritional requirements and ensuring a balanced diet."}{"title": "DIETA DE TRANSICI\u00d3N:La dieta de transici\u00f3n es el \u00faltimo paso en la progresi\u00f3n diet\u00e9tica, que incluye todos los grupos de alimentos y resulta en una dieta variada y equilibrada."}{"title": "DIETA DE F\u00c1CIL MASTICACI\u00d3N:The \"DIETA DE F\u00c1CIL MASTICACI\u00d3N\" is a specialized diet intended for patients who experience difficulties with chewing or salivating. This diet comprises a diverse, complete, and balanced array of soft-textured foods, ensuring that individuals can meet their nutritional needs despite their chewing challenges. It is specifically designed to accommodate the dietary requirements of those with masticatory or salivary issues, promoting both health and comfort in eating."}{"title": "PUR\u00c9 DE VERDURA:El pur\u00e9 de verdura es un alimento que se incluye en las dietas semil\u00edquidas y semiblandas, facilitando la digesti\u00f3n y la masticaci\u00f3n."}{"title": "PESCADO AL HORNO:El pescado al horno es un tipo de alimento que se introduce en la dieta semiblanda, siendo una fuente de prote\u00edna magra."}{"title": "FRUTA EN ALM\u00cdBAR:La fruta en alm\u00edbar es un tipo de postre que se incluye en las dietas semiblandas y blandas, proporcionando un sabor dulce y nutrientes."}{"title": "DIETAS CON MODIFICACI\u00d3N DE TEXTURA:Diets that involve changing the texture of food to accommodate patients with swallowing difficulties or other dietary restrictions."}{"title": "DIETA ODONTOLOGICA:A diet designed for patients with dental issues, focusing on soft foods that are easy to chew and swallow."}{"title": "QUESO FRESCO:QUESO FRESCO is a type of fresh cheese that is known for its soft and crumbly texture. It is often used in various culinary applications, particularly in Mexican cuisine. However, it is important to note that fresh cheese can be sticky, which may pose a risk for patients with dysphagia, a condition that affects swallowing. Therefore, caution should be exercised when serving QUESO FRESCO to individuals with this condition."}{"title": "CARAMELLOS:Candies that can be sticky and difficult to swallow, posing risks for patients with swallowing difficulties."}{"title": "HUEVO DURO:Hard-boiled eggs are a food that can be difficult to swallow without sauce, making them risky for patients with dysphagia."}{"title": "BISCOITOS:Biscuits are a type of food that can easily fragment, posing a risk for patients with swallowing difficulties."}{"title": "PATATAS CHIPS:Patatas chips, commonly known as potato chips, are a popular snack food characterized by their high fat and salt content. While they are enjoyed by many for their taste and crunch, it is important to note that these chips can easily fragment, which poses a risk for individuals with swallowing difficulties."}{"title": "BOMBONES RELLENOS:Filled chocolates that can release liquids when chewed, posing risks for patients with dysphagia."}{"title": "ACEITUNAS:Aceitunas, or olives, are a staple in Mediterranean diets and are recognized for their numerous health benefits. They are rich in oleic acid, which contributes to their nutritional value and association with healthy eating patterns. While aceitunas can be enjoyed in various culinary applications, it is important to note that they may contain pits, which can pose a risk for individuals with swallowing difficulties. Overall, aceitunas are a versatile food that plays a significant role in Mediterranean cuisine."}{"title": "UVAS:UVAS refers to grapes, a type of fruit that offers some dietary fiber. However, it is important to note that grapes can pose a choking hazard for patients with dysphagia, a condition that affects swallowing. Therefore, while UVAS can be a nutritious addition to the diet, caution should be exercised when they are consumed by individuals with swallowing difficulties."}{"title": "SAND\u00cdA:Sand\u00eda, commonly known as watermelon, is a type of fruit recognized for its high water content and sweetness. It is often enjoyed in various forms, including fresh slices, juiced, or incorporated into desserts. Additionally, Sand\u00eda contains a higher amount of galactose, which can be a consideration for certain dietary needs. It is important to note that watermelon can have seeds, which may pose a risk for individuals with swallowing difficulties."}{"title": "ESP\u00c1RRAGOS:Esp\u00e1rragos, or asparagus, are vegetables known for their nutritional benefits but also have certain characteristics that may pose risks for specific individuals. They contain hard fibers, which can be problematic for patients with dysphagia, a condition that makes swallowing difficult. Additionally, esp\u00e1rragos have moderate purine levels, which can influence uric acid levels in the body, potentially affecting individuals with conditions such as gout. Therefore, while esp\u00e1rragos can be a healthy addition to many diets, caution is advised for those with swallowing difficulties or issues related to uric acid."}{"title": "PUERROS:Puerros, commonly known as leeks, are a type of vegetable that contribute to dietary fiber intake. However, they are characterized by having hard fibers, which may pose a risk for patients with dysphagia, a condition that affects swallowing. Therefore, while puerros can be a nutritious addition to a diet, caution should be exercised when consumed by individuals with swallowing difficulties."}{"title": "FIBRAS DURAS:Hard fibers in foods that can pose risks for patients with swallowing difficulties."}{"title": "GRUMOS:Lumps in food that can pose risks for patients with dysphagia."}{"title": "HUESOS:HUESOS, or bones, are essential structures in the body that play a crucial role in providing support and protection to various organs. They are dependent on copper for their development and maintenance, highlighting the importance of this mineral in bone health. Additionally, certain types of bones can pose a choking hazard for patients with dysphagia, a condition that affects swallowing. This dual aspect of bones emphasizes their significance in both physiological functions and potential health risks."}{"title": "ESPINAS:Fish bones that can pose a choking hazard for patients with dysphagia."}{"title": "PEPITAS:Seeds that can pose a choking hazard for patients with dysphagia."}{"title": "CALDO VEGETAL:CALDO VEGETAL, or vegetable broth, is permitted in modified diets as part of the beverage group. It is particularly suitable for patients with swallowing difficulties, making it an important dietary option for those requiring specific nutritional considerations."}{"title": "MACEDONIA TRITURADA:Chopped fruit salad that is pureed for patients with swallowing difficulties."}{"title": "ACEITE OLIVA:ACEITE OLIVA is a type of oil characterized by its nutritional composition, which includes 13.5% saturated fats, 73.7% monounsaturated fats, and 8.4% polyunsaturated fats. This oil is particularly noted for its versatility, as it can be incorporated into diets for patients with swallowing difficulties, making it a suitable option for those requiring specific dietary considerations."}{"title": "CEREALES DEXTRINADOS:Dextrin cereals that can be included in diets for patients with swallowing difficulties."}{"title": "TORTILLA FRANCESA:The \"TORTILLA FRANCESA\" is a versatile dish that can be described as a gluten-free Spanish omelet, making it suitable for those following a gluten-free meal plan. Additionally, it is recognized as a French omelet that can be included in diets for patients with swallowing difficulties, highlighting its adaptability for various dietary needs."}{"title": "CHAMPIGNONES:Mushrooms that can be included in diets for patients with swallowing difficulties."}{"title": "MERIENDA:Merienda is an afternoon snack that plays a significant role in children's diets, typically comprising approximately 10-15% of their total caloric intake. This snack not only serves as a source of energy but also contributes to the daily nutritional needs of children. Additionally, merienda can be tailored to include specific items for dietary management, making it suitable for individuals with dietary restrictions. Overall, merienda is an important component of a balanced diet, providing both nourishment and enjoyment during the afternoon hours."}{"title": "COMIDA:Comida is recognized as the main meal of the day, playing a crucial role in contributing significantly to the total energy value of the diet. It is particularly important for individuals with dietary restrictions, as lunch can be tailored to include specific foods that meet their nutritional needs."}{"title": "CENA:CENA refers to the evening meal, which is an important part of daily nutrition. It should be balanced to meet the remaining nutritional needs of the day, ensuring that individuals receive adequate nourishment. For patients with dietary restrictions, CENA can include specific foods tailored to their needs, allowing for a safe and enjoyable dining experience. Additionally, for children, dinner should constitute approximately 25% of their total energy value for the day, highlighting its significance in their overall dietary intake."}{"title": "ALIMENTACI\u00d3N CON NUTRICI\u00d3N ARTIFICIAL:The use of artificial nutrition methods to provide essential nutrients to patients who cannot consume food normally."}{"title": "M\u00d3DULOS DE PROTE\u00cdNAS EN POLVO:Protein powder supplements used to enhance the protein content of meals for patients with specific dietary needs."}{"title": "PACIENTES CON QUEMADURAS:Patients suffering from severe burns who require specialized dietary plans to support healing and recovery."}{"title": "DIETA DE HEMODI\u00c1LISIS:A specific diet designed for patients undergoing hemodialysis, focusing on protein and mineral restrictions."}{"title": "DIETA 40 G/60 G PROTE\u00cdNAS:A dietary plan providing either 40 or 60 grams of protein, used for patients with renal and hepatic conditions."}{"title": "DIETAS CONTROL PROTEICO:Dietary plans specifically designed to manage protein intake for patients with various medical conditions."}{"title": "UPP CATAB\u00d3LICOS:A condition related to increased protein breakdown in the body, often requiring dietary adjustments."}{"title": "T\u00c9CNICAS DEPURACI\u00d3N EXTRARRENAL:Methods used to remove waste products from the blood in patients with kidney failure, influencing dietary needs."}{"title": "DIETA HEMODI\u00c1LISIS:A specific dietary regimen for patients undergoing hemodialysis, focusing on protein and mineral restrictions."}{"title": "DIETAS HIPOPROTEICAS:Dietas dise\u00f1adas para reducir la ingesta de prote\u00ednas y as\u00ed disminuir las concentraciones de urea en sangre y el s\u00edndrome ur\u00e9mico en pacientes con enfermedad renal"}{"title": "HEPATOPAT\u00cdA CR\u00d3NICA:HEPATOPAT\u00cdA CR\u00d3NICA, or chronic liver disease, is a medical condition characterized by long-term damage to the liver, which can result in liver dysfunction and potentially lead to liver failure. This condition often necessitates nutritional support due to the risk of malnutrition, which may arise from the disease itself. Patients with HEPATOPAT\u00cdA CR\u00d3NICA may experience complications such as malnutrition, encephalopathy, and sarcopenia, highlighting the importance of adequate nutritional intervention, including enteral feeding, to maintain health and manage the disease effectively."}{"title": "INSULIN THERAPY:Insulin therapy is a treatment for diabetes that involves administering insulin to control blood sugar levels, often requiring specific dietary adjustments."}{"title": "FIBER SOLUBLE:Soluble fiber is a type of fiber that can help regulate blood sugar levels and is recommended for diabetic diets."}{"title": "DIETARY RECOMMENDATIONS:Dietary recommendations encompass a variety of guidelines aimed at promoting overall health and managing specific medical conditions through balanced nutrition. These recommendations are designed to prevent atherosclerosis and enhance cardiovascular health, ensuring individuals maintain a heart-healthy diet. For patients with chronic kidney disease, dietary recommendations focus on managing phosphorus levels to support kidney function. \n\nIn the context of bariatric surgery, dietary recommendations provide essential guidelines for patients to follow post-operation, helping them achieve proper nutrition and maintain weight loss effectively. For individuals with Glycogen Storage Disease Type VI (GSDVI), dietary recommendations emphasize a high carbohydrate intake along with a slightly elevated protein intake to manage symptoms and sustain energy levels.\n\nFor those managing diabetes, dietary recommendations include guidelines that prioritize low sugar and high fiber intake to help regulate blood sugar levels. Additionally, these recommendations suggest a gradual reintroduction of lactose to assess tolerance in individuals who may be lactose intolerant. Furthermore, it is advised to limit foods high in fructose and sorbitol, particularly in processed products, to alleviate symptoms of intolerance. Overall, dietary recommendations serve as a crucial framework for individuals to achieve optimal health and manage specific dietary needs effectively."}{"title": "MEAL PLANS:Meal plans are structured dietary guidelines that help diabetic patients manage their food intake effectively."}{"title": "DIABETIC PATIENTS:Diabetic patients are individuals diagnosed with diabetes mellitus who require specific dietary management to control their condition."}{"title": "OBSTETRICIA:Obstetricia is the field of medicine that deals with childbirth and the care of women giving birth, which may include dietary management during pregnancy."}{"title": "ALUBIAS VERDES:Alubias verdes con patatas is a dish included in the laxative diet, consisting of green beans with potatoes, providing dietary fiber."}{"title": "MENESTRA DE VERDURAS:Menestra de verduras is a dish included in the laxative diet, consisting of a variety of vegetables, providing dietary fiber."}{"title": "PLANTAS DE GERIATR\u00cdA:Plantas de geriatr\u00eda are healthcare facilities that focus on elderly patients, often implementing specialized diets."}{"title": "TABLA 10:Tabla 10 refers to a specific table that details the content and distribution of carbohydrates in a diet of 1800 calories. Additionally, it includes a table that shows the contributions of vitamins in parenteral nutrition according to the age of pediatric patients. This comprehensive overview highlights both the carbohydrate distribution in a caloric context and the vitamin requirements tailored for different age groups in pediatric care."}{"title": "TABLA 11:Tabla 11 refers to a specific table outlining the components of a laxative diet."}{"title": "DIETA LAAXANTE:"}{"title": "DIETA POBRE EN RESIDUO:The \"DIETA POBRE EN RESIDUO\" is a specialized dietary regimen aimed at minimizing fecal volume to reduce the risk of intestinal obstruction, particularly indicated for patients with specific medical conditions. This low-residue diet is designed to limit the amount of undigested food that passes through the intestines, making it particularly beneficial for individuals suffering from certain gastrointestinal disorders. By focusing on reducing residue, the diet helps manage symptoms and improve overall digestive health for those affected."}{"title": "DIETA SIN RESIDUO:A diet designed to cleanse the intestines by excluding foods that form fecal matter, also indicated for specific medical tests."}{"title": "DIETA CONTROLADA EN GRASAS:A diet that regulates fat intake, used for diagnosing malabsorption and other related conditions."}{"title": "ACELGA CON PATATA:\"ACELGA CON PATATA\" is a dish that consists of Swiss chard and potatoes. It is recognized for its inclusion in various dietary plans, making it a versatile option for those seeking healthy meal choices. Additionally, this dish is gluten-free, making it suitable for individuals following a gluten-free diet."}{"title": "ENSALADA VERDE VARIADA:A varied green salad included in dietary recommendations."}{"title": "ENSALADA DE TOMATE Y QUESO FRESCO:The \"ENSALADA DE TOMATE Y QUESO FRESCO\" is a gluten-free salad that features a combination of fresh tomatoes and cheese. It is suitable for individuals following a gluten-free diet and is also included in various dietary plans. This salad is recognized for its simplicity and freshness, making it a versatile option for those seeking healthy meal choices."}{"title": "ENSALADA DEL CHEF:A chef's salad included in dietary recommendations."}{"title": "BORRAJA CON PATATA:\"BORRAJA CON PATATA\" is a dish that combines borage and potatoes, making it a nutritious option included in dietary recommendations. It is also gluten-free, which allows it to be part of a gluten-free meal plan, catering to those with gluten sensitivities or celiac disease. This dish not only highlights the unique flavor of borage but also provides a wholesome and healthy choice for various dietary needs."}{"title": "JUD\u00cdAS VERDES CON PATATA:A dish made of green beans and potatoes, included in dietary plans."}{"title": "HUEVOS AL GRAT\u00c9N:A dish of baked eggs, included in dietary recommendations."}{"title": "TOMATE ASADO:TOMATE ASADO is a gluten-free roasted tomato dish that is suitable for individuals following a gluten-free diet. It is often included in various dietary plans, making it a versatile option for those seeking healthy and flavorful meal choices."}{"title": "ABADEJO A LA GALLEGA:\"ABADEJO A LA GALLEGA\" is a dish of cod prepared in the traditional Galician style. It is recognized for its inclusion in dietary recommendations, highlighting its nutritional value. Additionally, this dish is gluten-free, making it suitable for those following a gluten-free meal plan."}{"title": "GUISANTES:Guisantes, commonly known as peas, are legumes that are valued for their sweet flavor and nutritional benefits. They are a gluten-free food, making them suitable for individuals following a gluten-free diet. Guisantes provide a notable amount of iron, offering 1.7 mg per 100 grams. Due to their versatility and health benefits, they are frequently included in various dietary plans."}{"title": "PLATIJA A LA ROMANA:A dish of sole prepared in the Roman style, included in dietary recommendations."}{"title": "MENESTRA:A mixed vegetable dish included in dietary plans."}{"title": "JAM\u00d3N ASADO EN SALSA:JAM\u00d3N ASADO EN SALSA is a gluten-free roasted ham dish served with sauce, making it a suitable option for those following a gluten-free meal plan. This dish is also included in dietary recommendations, highlighting its nutritional value and compatibility with various dietary needs."}{"title": "PESCADILLA A LA MARINERA:A dish of fish prepared in a sailor's style, included in dietary recommendations."}{"title": "KIWI:Kiwi is a small, brown, fuzzy fruit characterized by its bright green flesh and tiny black seeds. It is renowned for its unique sweet and tangy flavor, making it a popular choice among fruit lovers. The kiwi fruit is rich in dietary fiber and is included in dietary recommendations due to its numerous health benefits. It contains a significant amount of vitamin C, contributing to its nutritional value. Additionally, kiwi has a fructose content of 4-5 grams per 100 grams and a higher amount of galactose, ranging from 10-20 mg per 100 grams. Overall, kiwi is celebrated not only for its distinctive taste but also for its health-promoting properties."}{"title": "DESCAFEINADO:Decaffeinated coffee included in dietary recommendations."}{"title": "MERMELADA CIRUELA:Plum jam included in dietary plans."}{"title": "SUFICIENTE CANTIDAD DE L\u00cdQUIDOS:The recommendation to ensure adequate liquid intake for health management."}{"title": "OBSTRUCCI\u00d3N DEL DRENAJE LINF\u00c1TICO:A medical condition that may require dietary management."}{"title": "TRASTORNOS DEL METABOLISMO LIPOPROTEICO:A condition that may necessitate dietary adjustments for health management."}{"title": "PREPARACI\u00d3N DE PRUEBAS RADIOGR\u00c1FICAS:The process of preparing for radiological tests that may require specific dietary restrictions."}{"title": "DIETA POBRE EN GRASAS/ALIP\u00cdDICA:A diet low in fats, indicated for patients with certain medical conditions.)<|COMPLETE|>"}{"title": "ASOCIACI\u00d3N ESPA\u00d1OLA DE CEL\u00cdACOS:The Asociaci\u00f3n Espa\u00f1ola de Cel\u00edacos is an organization that authorizes foods suitable for a gluten-free diet for patients with celiac disease."}{"title": "CELIAQU\u00cdA:CELIAQU\u00cdA, also known as Celiac Disease, is an autoimmune disorder characterized by an adverse reaction to gluten, a protein found in wheat, barley, and rye. This condition necessitates a strict gluten-free diet to effectively manage symptoms and prevent potential complications. Ongoing research suggests that there may be potential links between probiotic treatment and the management of Celiac Disease, indicating a possible area for future therapeutic exploration. Overall, CELIAQU\u00cdA requires careful dietary management to ensure the health and well-being of those affected."}{"title": "DIETA SIN GLUTEN:\"DIETA SIN GLUTEN\" refers to a dietary model that excludes gluten, which is essential for the health of individuals with celiac disease and those with non-celiac gluten sensitivity. This gluten-free diet involves the complete elimination of foods containing gluten grains, making it a crucial treatment for celiac patients. The diet is designed to be nutritionally complete and includes a variety of meals for each day of the week, encompassing breakfast, lunch, and dinner options. Overall, \"DIETA SIN GLUTEN\" serves as a vital dietary regimen tailored to meet the specific needs of those affected by gluten-related disorders."}{"title": "DIETA POBRE EN PURINAS:The \"DIETA POBRE EN PURINAS\" is a dietary model specifically designed to limit purine intake, primarily aimed at patients suffering from gout. This diet includes specific meal recommendations that help manage and reduce uric acid levels in individuals with hyperuricemia. In addition to dietary management, the low-purine diet emphasizes the importance of weight reduction as a means to further alleviate symptoms and improve overall health for those affected by these conditions."}{"title": "PACIENTES CEL\u00cdACOS:Patients with celiac disease who require a gluten-free diet to avoid symptoms and complications."}{"title": "DIETA CON 100 GR DE GRASA:A diet that includes 100 grams of fat, which may be used for specific nutritional needs or conditions."}{"title": "DIETA POBRE EN GRASA:A low-fat diet is designed to limit fat intake, often recommended for patients with specific health conditions."}{"title": "DIETA OVO-LACTO-VEGETARIANA:A vegetarian diet that includes both eggs and dairy products, considered the most inclusive among vegetarian diets."}{"title": "DIETA PARA NEUTROPENIA:A specialized diet for patients undergoing chemotherapy or bone marrow transplants, aimed at reducing the risk of infection by avoiding high-risk foods."}{"title": "ALUBIAS VERDES CON PATATA:A gluten-free meal consisting of green beans and potatoes, featured in the gluten-free diet."}{"title": "POTAJES DE GARBANZOS:A gluten-free dish made with chickpeas, part of the gluten-free meal plan."}{"title": "PASTA CON TOMATE SIN GLUTEN:A gluten-free pasta dish served with tomato sauce, included in the gluten-free diet."}{"title": "ARROZ VEGETAL SIN GLUTEN:A gluten-free rice dish with vegetables, featured in the gluten-free diet."}{"title": "ESTOFADO DE TERNEA:A gluten-free beef stew, part of the gluten-free meal plan."}{"title": "POLLO JARDINERA:A gluten-free chicken dish with vegetables, included in the gluten-free diet."}{"title": "BACALAO T\u00cdA TERE:A gluten-free cod dish, featured in the gluten-free meal plan."}{"title": "ENSALADA LOMO BRASEADO:A gluten-free salad with braised pork, part of the gluten-free diet."}{"title": "PIMIENTOS ESTOFADO DE PAVO:A gluten-free dish made with peppers and turkey, included in the gluten-free meal plan."}{"title": "GRANADERO A LA VASCA:A gluten-free dish made with a specific type of fish, featured in the gluten-free diet."}{"title": "TOMATE NATURAL:A gluten-free natural tomato dish, part of the gluten-free meal plan."}{"title": "POLLO AL CHILINDR\u00d3N:A gluten-free chicken dish cooked in a red sauce, included in the gluten-free diet."}{"title": "POSTRE L\u00c1CTEO SIN GLUTEN:A gluten-free dairy dessert, included in the gluten-free diet plan."}{"title": "FRUTA NATURAL:Natural fruit served as part of the gluten-free diet, included twice a week."}{"title": "PAN SIN GLUTEN:Gluten-free bread included in the diet plan."}{"title": "PUR\u00c9 DE BORRAJA CON PATATA:A gluten-free puree made with borage and potatoes, part of the gluten-free meal plan."}{"title": "JUD\u00cdAS VERDES PATATA:A gluten-free dish made with green beans and potatoes, included in the gluten-free diet."}{"title": "ARROZ PILAF:A gluten-free pilaf rice dish, included in the gluten-free diet."}{"title": "PATATA PANADERA:A gluten-free baked potato dish, included in the gluten-free diet."}{"title": "PESCADILLA SALSA SIN GLUTEN:A gluten-free fish dish served with sauce, part of the gluten-free meal plan."}{"title": "AGUA MINERAL ALCALINA:Alkaline mineral water recommended for hydration in the dietary plans."}{"title": "AGUA MINERAL:Mineral water recommended for hydration in the dietary plans.)<|COMPLETE|>"}{"title": "ONCOLOGY SAFE-HANDLING DIET:A dietary guideline aimed at minimizing infection risk for patients with specific health conditions by outlining safe food handling practices."}{"title": "DIETA ESPECIAL/NO CODIFICADA/PERSONALIZADA:A personalized diet plan for patients who cannot follow a standard diet due to various reasons, requiring assessment by nutrition professionals."}{"title": "DIETA OVOLACTOVEGETARIANA:A vegetarian diet that includes eggs and dairy products, designed to provide balanced nutrition while avoiding meat."}{"title": "RECOMENDACIONES GENERALES:General dietary recommendations for patients with esophagogastric diets, focusing on meal timing, portion sizes, and food choices."}{"title": "PROTECCI\u00d3N G\u00c1STRICA:A dietary approach aimed at minimizing mechanical and chemical stimulation of the stomach, often involving low-fiber and low-acid foods."}{"title": "PROTECCI\u00d3N BILIAR:A dietary strategy that reduces fat intake to support gallbladder health, often involving low-fat dairy and simple cooking methods."}{"title": "NUTRITIONAL CONTROL:Nutritional control for patients undergoing bariatric surgery aims to ensure adequate intake, limit complications, and address nutritional deficits."}{"title": "LIQUID DIET:The \"LIQUID DIET\" refers to a specific dietary phase that is commonly implemented following bariatric surgery. This diet involves the consumption of only liquids, which is crucial for aiding recovery and adaptation after the surgical procedure. The primary purpose of the liquid diet is to protect the surgical sites and facilitate healing. It is characterized by small volumes of liquid intake, ensuring that patients can gradually reintroduce food while minimizing the risk of complications. Additionally, a liquid diet can also be prescribed for patients with certain medical conditions, emphasizing its role in various therapeutic contexts. Overall, the liquid diet serves as an essential step in the post-operative care of bariatric surgery patients, focusing on liquid or liquid-form foods to support their recovery process."}{"title": "SOLID DIET:A solid diet is the final phase of dietary reintroduction after bariatric surgery, transitioning from liquids to solid foods."}{"title": "SUPPLEMENTAL NUTRITION:Supplemental nutrition includes additional nutritional products provided to patients to meet dietary needs post-surgery."}{"title": "YOGURT:Yogurt is a dairy product that serves as a nutritious option for patients, particularly those who are lactose intolerant. It is a fermented dairy product that not only provides essential calcium but also allows individuals to enjoy a source of nutrition while minimizing lactose intake."}{"title": "LEGUMES:Legumes are a category of plant foods recognized for their nutritional benefits, particularly their high protein and fiber content, which contribute positively to cardiovascular health. They are frequently highlighted in dietary guidelines, emphasizing their favorable phosphorus-to-protein ratio, making them suitable for renal patients. However, it is important to note that legumes are restricted in the diets of individuals who need to limit their potassium intake, as they contain high levels of potassium. Overall, legumes play a significant role in nutrition, but their consumption should be tailored to individual dietary needs, especially for those with specific health conditions."}{"title": "\u00c1NGEL MANUEL CARACUEL GARC\u00cdA:\u00c1ngel Manuel Caracuel Garc\u00eda is an author known for his work on the normalization of hospital food and nutrition."}{"title": "CAMPFR\u00cdO FOOD GROUP:Campofr\u00edo Food Group is a food company that specializes in the production and distribution of processed meat products. In addition to its core business, the company has also published works on hospital nutrition and food standards, indicating its commitment to promoting health and quality in food consumption."}{"title": "D\u00cdAZ DE SANTOS:D\u00edaz de Santos is a prominent publishing company based in Spain, recognized for its extensive range of academic and professional publications. The company specializes in educational literature, with a particular focus on medical and nutritional topics. Among its notable works is the \"Manual de Nutrici\u00f3n Cl\u00ednica y Diet\u00e9tica,\" which highlights its commitment to providing valuable resources in the field of nutrition. Overall, D\u00edaz de Santos is well-regarded for its contributions to both academic and professional literature, particularly in the areas of health and education."}{"title": "NUTRITION UNIT:The Nutrition Unit is a department within hospitals responsible for overseeing dietary plans and ensuring they meet patients' nutritional needs."}{"title": "ONCOLOGICAL TREATMENT:Oncological treatment refers to medical care provided to patients with cancer, which may require specific dietary considerations."}{"title": "DIABETIC DEBUT:Diabetic debut refers to the initial onset of diabetes in a patient, during which dietary education and management are crucial."}{"title": "FOOD ALLERGIES:Food allergies are adverse reactions to certain foods that must be documented and managed in a hospital setting to ensure patient safety."}{"title": "NUTRITIONAL SUPPLEMENTS:Nutritional supplements are additional nutrients provided to patients when their dietary intake is insufficient for their health needs. They are particularly recommended for patients post-bariatric surgery to ensure adequate protein and nutrient intake. These products are also intended to enhance the diet of individuals with specific health conditions, such as cancer and diabetes, to improve nutritional intake and support recovery. Nutritional supplements are commonly used in clinical settings for patients with specific nutritional needs, offering a means to provide essential vitamins, minerals, and trace elements that may be lacking in their regular diet. Overall, nutritional supplements play a crucial role in enhancing dietary intake and ensuring that individuals receive the necessary nutrients for optimal health."}{"title": "HYPERCHOLESTEROLEMIA:Hypercholesterolemia is a condition of elevated cholesterol levels in the blood, which may require dietary modifications."}{"title": "CARDIOVASCULAR ISSUES:Cardiovascular issues refer to health problems related to the heart and blood vessels, often requiring dietary adjustments."}{"title": "FOOD INTOLERANCES:Food intolerances refer to adverse reactions to specific foods that do not engage the immune system. These intolerances often require individuals to make dietary modifications to avoid discomfort and other related symptoms."}{"title": "CODES OF DIETS:Codes of diets are protocols established in hospitals that outline various dietary options available for patients."}{"title": "MANUAL DE NUTRICI\u00d3N Y METABOLISMO:Manual de Nutrici\u00f3n y Metabolismo is a publication that provides comprehensive information on nutrition and metabolism."}{"title": "MANUAL DE NUTRICI\u00d3N CL\u00cdNICA Y DIET\u00c9TICA:Manual de Nutrici\u00f3n Cl\u00ednica y Diet\u00e9tica is a publication that focuses on clinical nutrition and dietary practices."}{"title": "ALFONSO VIDAL CASARIEGO:Alfonso Vidal Casariego is a distinguished medical professional specializing in endocrinology and nutrition, with a significant focus on the treatment of obesity. He serves as a researcher in clinical nutrition at the Clinical Nutrition Unit of the University Hospital of Le\u00f3n. In addition to his clinical work, Alfonso Vidal Casariego is also an author in the field of clinical nutrition and dietetics, contributing valuable insights and knowledge to the discipline."}{"title": "ALICIA CALLEJA FERN\u00c1NDEZ:Alicia Calleja Fern\u00e1ndez is a medical professional specializing in endocrinology and nutrition, with a focus on the treatment of obesity. She is also a researcher in the field of clinical nutrition and dietetics, affiliated with the Clinical Nutrition Unit at the University Hospital of Le\u00f3n. Through her work, she contributes significantly to advancing knowledge and practices in nutrition and obesity management."}{"title": "GEORGIOS KYRIAKOS:Georgios Kyriakos is a medical professional specializing in endocrinology and nutrition, contributing to the treatment of obesity."}{"title": "TRATAMIENTO FARMACOL\u00d3GICO DE LA OBESIDAD:Tratamiento farmacol\u00f3gico de la obesidad refers to the pharmacological treatment of obesity, which is a topic covered in the document."}{"title": "TRATAMIENTO QUIR\u00daRGICO DE LA OBESIDAD:Tratamiento quir\u00fargico de la obesidad refers to surgical treatment options for obesity, which is discussed in the document."}{"title": "FESNAD-SEEDO:FESNAD-SEEDO is a consensus organization dedicated to outlining dietary management strategies for obesity. It provides nutritional recommendations aimed at the prevention and treatment of overweight and obesity in adults. Through its guidelines, FESNAD-SEEDO seeks to promote effective dietary practices to address these significant health concerns."}{"title": "AMERICAN ASSOCIATION OF CLINICAL ENDOCRINOLOGIST:The American Association of Clinical Endocrinologists is a professional organization dedicated to advancing the field of endocrinology. It plays a crucial role in providing guidelines for the diagnosis and treatment of obesity and related conditions. Additionally, the organization offers alternative classifications for obesity that take into account body mass index (BMI) and associated comorbidities, thereby enhancing the understanding and management of this complex health issue."}{"title": "SOCIOECONOMIC CHANGES:Socioeconomic changes refer to shifts in economic and social factors that have increased food availability and contributed to obesity."}{"title": "SLEEP APNEA:Sleep apnea is a disorder that can be exacerbated by obesity, characterized by interrupted breathing during sleep."}{"title": "OSTEOARTHRITIS:Osteoarthritis is a degenerative joint disease that can be influenced by obesity due to increased weight on joints."}{"title": "BODY COMPOSITION TECHNIQUES:Body composition techniques are methods used to assess body fat percentage and diagnose obesity."}{"title": "CIRCUMFERENCE MEASUREMENT:Circumference measurement is an anthropometric method used to assess obesity risk based on waist size."}{"title": "WEIGHT MANAGEMENT:Weight management involves strategies and practices aimed at maintaining a healthy weight, particularly in the context of obesity. It refers to the process of adopting long-term lifestyle modifications to achieve and sustain a healthy weight. This encompasses various approaches, including dietary changes, physical activity, and behavioral adjustments, all designed to promote overall health and prevent weight-related issues."}{"title": "ENERGY INTAKE:Energy intake refers to the amount of calories consumed, which is crucial for managing diabetes and maintaining a healthy weight."}{"title": "AMERICAN COLLEGE OF ENDOCRINOLOGY:The American College of Endocrinology is a professional organization dedicated to the treatment and management of endocrine disorders, with a particular emphasis on obesity. It collaborates with the American Association of Clinical Endocrinologists to develop and provide guidelines for effective obesity management, ensuring that healthcare professionals have access to the latest standards and practices in the field."}{"title": "SINDROME METABOLICO:Metabolic syndrome is a cluster of conditions that increase the risk of heart disease, stroke, and diabetes, often associated with obesity."}{"title": "HIPERTENSION:Hypertension, or high blood pressure, is a common condition that can be exacerbated by obesity."}{"title": "HIGADO GRASO NO ALCOHOLICO:Non-alcoholic fatty liver disease is a condition where fat builds up in the liver, often associated with obesity and metabolic syndrome."}{"title": "MUJERES JOVENES SANAS:Young healthy women are one of the identified groups of individuals that may require specific obesity treatment approaches."}{"title": "VARONES BEBEDORES SEVEROS DE ALCOHOL:Severe alcohol-consuming men are another group identified that may face unique challenges in obesity treatment."}{"title": "PERSONAS DE MEDIANA EDAD CON ANSIEDAD:Middle-aged individuals with anxiety are identified as a group that may require tailored obesity treatment strategies."}{"title": "ANCIANOS SALUDABLES CON RECURSOS:Healthy elderly individuals with resources are another demographic that may need specific obesity management approaches."}{"title": "ANCIANOS CON ENFERMEDADES CR\u00d3NICAS:Elderly individuals with chronic diseases but without psychological issues are also a group that may require specialized obesity treatment."}{"title": "PACIENTES CON PEOR SALUD:Patients in poor health are identified as a group that may face significant challenges in managing obesity."}{"title": "APNEA DEL SUE\u00d1O:APNEA DEL SUE\u00d1O is a condition characterized by repeated interruptions in breathing during sleep, which can significantly affect overall health. It is often associated with obesity, making it a relevant consideration in the context of very low-calorie diets (VLCD). This relationship highlights the importance of addressing sleep apnea in individuals who are managing obesity, as it can be a comorbid condition that complicates health outcomes."}{"title": "TRASTORNOS PSICOL\u00d3GICOS:Psychological disorders can influence obesity treatment outcomes, as they may affect motivation and adherence to treatment plans."}{"title": "REGISTROS DIET\u00c9TICOS:Dietary records are used to track food intake over time, aiding in the management of obesity."}{"title": "CUESTIONARIOS PREDEFINIDOS:Predefined questionnaires are tools used to assess dietary habits and energy intake, important for obesity treatment."}{"title": "BALANCE ENERG\u00c9TICO:Energy balance refers to the relationship between calories consumed and calories expended, crucial for weight management."}{"title": "OBJETIVOS DE TRATAMIENTO:Treatment objectives are specific goals set for weight loss and health improvement in patients with obesity.)<|COMPLETE|>"}{"title": "H\u00cdGADO GRASO NO ALCOH\u00d3LICO:H\u00edgado Graso No Alcoh\u00f3lico, also known as non-alcoholic fatty liver disease (NAFLD), is a medical condition characterized by the accumulation of fat in the liver. This condition typically occurs in individuals who consume little or no alcohol. It can be associated with various factors, including iron overload. The presence of excess fat in the liver can lead to further complications if not managed properly."}{"title": "APNEA OBSTRUCTIVA DEL SUE\u00d1O:Obstructive sleep apnea is a potentially serious sleep disorder in which breathing repeatedly stops and starts during sleep."}{"title": "ASTMA:Asthma is a condition in which your airways narrow and swell and may produce extra mucus, making breathing difficult."}{"title": "OSTEOARTRITIS:Osteoarthritis is a degenerative joint disease that occurs when the protective cartilage that cushions the ends of the bones wears down over time."}{"title": "INCONTINENCIA URINARIA:Urinary incontinence is the involuntary leakage of urine, which can be a result of various underlying conditions."}{"title": "DENSIDAD ENERG\u00c9TICA:Energy density refers to the number of calories in a given volume or weight of food, influencing dietary choices and weight management."}{"title": "P\u00c9NDULO DE PESO:Weight pendulum refers to the concept of maintaining a stable weight through balanced energy intake and expenditure."}{"title": "DIRECTIVA 98/6/CE:Directiva 98/6/CE es una regulaci\u00f3n de la Comisi\u00f3n Europea que establece normas sobre la composici\u00f3n, etiquetado y duraci\u00f3n de uso de productos de muy bajo contenido cal\u00f3rico."}{"title": "REAL DECRETO 1430/1997:El Real Decreto 1430/1997 es la incorporaci\u00f3n al ordenamiento jur\u00eddico espa\u00f1ol de la Directiva 98/6/CE, regulando productos de muy bajo contenido cal\u00f3rico."}{"title": "PACIENTES ADULTOS OBESOS:Pacientes adultos obesos son aquellos que tienen un \u00edndice de masa corporal (IMC) superior a 30 kg/m\u00b2 y que han fracasado en intentos previos de p\u00e9rdida de peso."}{"title": "ENFERMEDADES CARD\u00cdACAS:Las enfermedades card\u00edacas son condiciones que afectan el coraz\u00f3n y pueden ser contraindicaciones para el uso de dietas VLCD."}{"title": "SOBREPESO GRADO II:El sobrepeso grado II se refiere a un IMC superior a 27 kg/m\u00b2 y puede estar asociado a comorbilidades que justifican el uso de dietas VLCD."}{"title": "TRASTORNOS PSIQUI\u00c1TRICOS:TRASTORNOS PSIQUI\u00c1TRICOS se refiere a condiciones de salud mental que pueden influir en el tratamiento y la nutrici\u00f3n de los pacientes. Estas condiciones son consideradas contraindicaciones para el uso de dietas de muy bajo contenido cal\u00f3rico (VLCD). Adem\u00e1s, trastornos psiqui\u00e1tricos como la depresi\u00f3n cl\u00ednica son comunes en pacientes que padecen enfermedades cr\u00f3nicas severas, lo que puede afectar negativamente su ingesta nutricional."}{"title": "ANOREXIA/BULIMIA:La anorexia y la bulimia son trastornos alimentarios que son contraindicaciones para el uso de dietas VLCD."}{"title": "INGESTA CAL\u00d3RICA:La ingesta cal\u00f3rica se refiere a la cantidad de calor\u00edas consumidas a trav\u00e9s de los alimentos, que puede aumentar con alimentos de alta densidad energ\u00e9tica."}{"title": "PALATABILIDAD:La palatabilidad se refiere a la aceptaci\u00f3n y el placer que se experimenta al consumir alimentos, a menudo influenciada por el contenido de grasa."}{"title": "ESTUDIOS DE INTERVENCI\u00d3N:Los estudios de intervenci\u00f3n son investigaciones que analizan el efecto de modificar la densidad energ\u00e9tica en la dieta sobre la p\u00e9rdida de peso."}{"title": "PRODUCTOS COMERCIALES:Los productos comerciales son alimentos dise\u00f1ados para ser utilizados en dietas de muy bajo contenido cal\u00f3rico, como barritas y galletas."}{"title": "M\u00c1S DE 12 KCAL/KG:M\u00e1s de 12 kcal/kg se refiere a la cantidad de calor\u00edas que se considera alta en comparaci\u00f3n con las dietas de muy bajo contenido cal\u00f3rico."}{"title": "M\u00c1S BARATOS:Los alimentos energ\u00e9ticamente m\u00e1s densos suelen ser m\u00e1s baratos, lo que puede influir en las decisiones de consumo."}{"title": "MOTIVOS DE SALUD:Los motivos de salud son razones que pueden justificar la necesidad de una p\u00e9rdida de peso r\u00e1pida, como condiciones m\u00e9dicas."}ø¿0␀␀␀␀␀~¡0␀␀␀␀␀¬0␀␀␀␀␀“¬0␀␀␀␀␀t√0␀␀␀␀␀)ƒ0␀␀␀␀␀æ≈0␀␀␀␀␀.»0␀␀␀␀␀…0␀␀␀␀␀Œ…0␀␀␀␀␀£ 0␀␀␀␀␀bÀ0␀␀␀␀␀ûÀ0␀␀␀␀␀gÃ0␀␀␀␀␀ÛÃ0␀␀␀␀␀{Œ0␀␀␀␀␀œ0␀␀␀␀␀∂œ0␀␀␀␀␀ä–0␀␀␀␀␀3—0␀␀␀␀␀Í—0␀␀␀␀␀ì“0␀␀␀␀␀)”0␀␀␀␀␀Õ”0␀␀␀␀␀—‘0␀␀␀␀␀b’0␀␀␀␀␀÷0␀␀␀␀␀‹ÿ0␀␀␀␀␀∞⁄0␀␀␀␀␀a€0␀␀␀␀␀‹0␀␀␀␀␀≈‹0␀␀␀␀␀Ö›0␀␀␀␀␀ﬁ0␀␀␀␀␀Æﬁ0␀␀␀␀␀xﬂ0␀␀␀␀␀2‡0␀␀␀␀␀·0␀␀␀␀␀Â·0␀␀␀␀␀}‚0␀␀␀␀␀/„0␀␀␀␀␀œ„0␀␀␀␀␀{‰0␀␀␀␀␀Â0␀␀␀␀␀ÉÂ0␀␀␀␀␀Ê0␀␀␀␀␀ãÊ0␀␀␀␀␀Á0␀␀␀␀␀ÉÁ0␀␀␀␀␀6Ë0␀␀␀␀␀ÿË0␀␀␀␀␀^È0␀␀␀␀␀‰È0␀␀␀␀␀˝È0␀␀␀␀␀ŒÍ0␀␀␀␀␀SÎ0␀␀␀␀␀◊Î0␀␀␀␀␀XÏ0␀␀␀␀␀MÌ0␀␀␀␀␀àÌ0␀␀␀␀␀JÓ0␀␀␀␀␀àÔ0␀␀␀␀␀bÒ0␀␀␀␀␀Û0␀␀␀␀␀ı0␀␀␀␀␀{ı0␀␀␀␀␀⁄ı0␀␀␀␀␀)ˆ0␀␀␀␀␀•ˆ0␀␀␀␀␀/˜0␀␀␀␀␀R¯0␀␀␀␀␀Ç˙0␀␀␀␀␀‰˝0␀␀␀␀␀dˇ0␀␀␀␀␀␀1␀␀␀␀␀n1␀␀␀␀␀)1␀␀␀␀␀ﬂ1